window.__VD__=window.__VD__||{};window.__VD__["n"]={"neglect":[["nɪˈɡlekt","nɪˈɡlekt"],["CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["复数","neglects"],["原形","neglect"],["第三人称单数","neglects"],["现在分词","neglecting"],["过去式","neglected"],["过去分词","neglected"],["名词","neglecter",1],["形容词","neglectful",1],["副词","neglectfully",1],["名词","neglectfulness",1]],[15,3.0,13,7,6],[["v.","疏于照顾；未予看管",1],["v.","忽略；忽视；不予重视",9],["v.","疏忽；疏漏",0],["n.","忽略；忽视；未被重视",5]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","Asia is arguably the region most neglected by global efforts to increase diversity in restoration and to study native species.","在全球增加生态恢复多样性、研究本地物种的努力中，亚洲或许是最受忽视的地区。","正文"],["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","For millennia, we’ve known what we’ve known due to artifacts that have survived, often despite their original creators’ neglect.","几千年来，我们之所以知道过去的事，是因为一些物件留存了下来，而它们往往是在原制作者疏于照管的情况下幸存的。","正文"],["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","But the effects of the heat were amplified by humidity — an often neglected factor in heat alert systems — and the lack of shade at the late-morning outdoor ceremony.","但湿度以及上午较晚时段的露天仪式缺少遮阴处，使高温的影响加剧；湿度往往是高温预警系统忽视的因素。","正文"],["2017 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","On the other hand, Tronick himself is concerned that the worries about kids’ use of screens are born out of an “oppressive ideology that demands that parents should always be interacting” with their children: “It’s based on a somewhat fantasised, very white, very upper-middle-class ideology that says if you’re failing to expose your child to 30,000 words you are neglecting them.”","另一方面，特罗尼克本人担心，人们对孩子使用屏幕的忧虑源于一种“要求父母始终与孩子互动的压迫性观念”。他说：“它建立在一种多少有些幻想色彩、极具白人及中上阶层色彩的观念之上：如果你没让孩子接触三万个词，就是忽视了他们。”","正文"],["2013 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","But the intention is not to neglect social science; rather, the complete opposite.","但其本意并非忽视社会科学，恰恰相反。","正文"],["2011 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","(48) This seems a justification for neglect of those in need, and a rationalization of exploitation, of the superiority of those at the top and the inferiority of those at the bottom.","（48）这似乎是在为忽视需要帮助的人找借口，也是在为剥削、为上层人的优越和底层人的低下提供合理化解释。","正文"]],"neglect.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neg- = deny, 表示“否认”，原始印欧语形式为 *ne- (no, not)，和词根 un- 同源。"],["词根","lect-,lig-,leg- = choose, gather, 表示“选择，收集”，来自拉丁语。"]],"d":[["neglected","被忽视的"],["neglectful","疏忽的"]]}],"negligible":[["ˈneɡ.lɪ.dʒə.bᵊl","ˈneɡ·lɪ·dʒə·bəl"],["CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["名词","negligibility",1],["副词","negligibly",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["adj.","微不足道的；不重要的；不值一提的",0]],[],"negligible.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neg- = deny, 表示“否认”，原始印欧语形式为 *ne- (no, not)，和词根 un- 同源。"],["词根","lect-,lig-,leg- = choose, gather, 表示“选择，收集”，来自拉丁语。"],["后缀","-ible 表形容词，“能…的”。"]],"d":[]}],"necessary":[["ˈnes.ə.ser.i","ˈnes·əˌser·i"],["中考","高中"],[["复数","necessaries"],["名词","necessariness",1],["形容词","unnecessary",1],["副词","unnecessarily",1],["名词","unnecessariness",1]],[34,4.0,23,23,0],[["adj.","必需的；必要的",33],["adj.","必然的；无法避免的",1]],[["2024 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","Sue Rexford, the director of college guidance at the Charles E. Smith Jewish Day School, says it is not necessary for a student filling out the Common Application to list 10 activities in the application.","查尔斯·E.史密斯犹太日校的升学指导主任苏·雷克斯福德说，学生填写通用申请表时，不必列出十项活动。","正文"],["2023 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Scopus itself has all the data necessary to detect this malpractice.","Scopus本身掌握着检测这种不当行为所需的全部数据。","正文"],["2023 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","“As the marketplace adapts to the new requirements, and the technologies that support them, the scaling up of these technologies will eventually bring costs down, but in the short term, we will all have to pay the price of the necessary transition,” he says.","他说：‘随着市场适应新要求和支撑这些要求的技术，这些技术的规模化最终会降低成本；但在短期内，我们都必须为必要的转型付出代价。’","正文"],["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","The reach of art-science tie-ups needs to go beyond the necessary purpose of research communication, and participants must not fall into the trap of stereotyping each other.","艺术与科学合作的影响不应止于科研传播这一必要目的，参与者也不能陷入相互贴标签的陷阱。","正文"],["2020 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","But are such government mandates even necessary?","但这样的政府强制规定真的有必要吗？","正文"],["2020 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","“We’d assumed we’d have to give it a moving head and tail, facial features, and put a scent on it to make it smell like a real rat, but that wasn’t necessary,” says Janet Wiles at the University of Queensland in Australia, who helped with the research.","参与研究的澳大利亚昆士兰大学的珍妮特·怀尔斯说：“我们原以为必须给它装上会动的头和尾巴、添上面部特征，再给它弄上气味，让它闻起来像真老鼠，但事实证明没有这个必要。”","正文"]],"necessary.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neg- = deny, 表示“否认”，原始印欧语形式为 *ne- (no, not)，和词根 un- 同源。"],["词根","ced-,ceed-,cess- = go away; withdraw, yield, 表示“走开，撤退，屈服”。来自拉丁语。"],["后缀","-ary 表形容词，“…的”。"]],"d":[["necessity","n. 必要(性); (迫切)需要 必需品 自然规律"],["necessarily","adv. 必要地, 必需地 必定地; 必然地"],["unnecessary","adj. 不必要的, 多余的"],["necessitate","vt. 使…成为必要, 需要；迫使"],["unnecessarily","adv. 不必要地;多余地;不需要地"]]}],"necessitate":[["nəˈses.ɪ.teɪt","nəˈses·ɪˌteɪt"],["CET6","考研","IELTS"],[["原形","necessitate"],["第三人称单数","necessitates"],["现在分词","necessitating"],["过去式","necessitated"],["过去分词","necessitated"],["名词","necessitation",1]],[1,0.5,1,0,0],[["v.","使成为必要",1]],[["2018 英一 · 阅读 · Part B · 选项G","In 1866, the construction of the North Wing of the Treasury Building necessitated the demolition of the State Department building.","1866年，财政部大楼北翼的建设迫使人们拆除国务院大楼。",""]],"necessitate.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neg- = deny, 表示“否认”，原始印欧语形式为 *ne- (no, not)，和词根 un- 同源。"],["词根","ced-,ceed-,cess- = go away; withdraw, yield, 表示“走开，撤退，屈服”。来自拉丁语。"],["后缀","-ary 表形容词，“…的”。"],["后缀","-ate 表动词，“做，造成”。"]],"d":[]}],"necessity":[["nəˈses.ə.ti","nəˈses·ɪ·t̬i"],["CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL"],[["复数","necessities"]],[12,2.5,11,3,5],[["n.","必然；必要；需要",8],["n.","必需的事物；必需品",3],["n.","必然性；不可避免的情况",1]],[["2017 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","At the same time, people continue to treat fire as an event that needs to be wholly controlled and unleashed only out of necessity, says Professor Balch at the University of Colorado.","科罗拉多大学的鲍尔奇教授说，与此同时，人们仍把火视为一种必须完全控制、只有在必要时才能让它燃烧的现象。","正文"],["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","Of necessity, colonial America was a projection of Europe.","殖民时期的美洲必然是欧洲的延伸。","正文"],["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Orin Kerr, a law professor, compares the explosion and accessibility of digital information in the 21st century with the establishment of automobile use as a virtual necessity of life in the 20th: The justices had to specify novel rules for the new personal domain of the passenger car then; they must sort out how the Fourth Amendment applies to digital information now.","法学教授奥林·克尔将21世纪数字信息的激增与获取便捷，比作20世纪汽车逐渐成为生活中几乎不可缺少的东西：当年，大法官们不得不针对作为新私人空间的乘用汽车制定新规则；如今，他们必须厘清第四修正案如何适用于数字信息。","正文"],["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4 · 第36题 · 选项B","According to Paragraph 1, desire paths are a result of the necessity to preserve green spaces.","根据第一段，愿望路径的形成源于保护绿地的需要。","选项"],["2023 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2 · 第29题 · 选项C","What does Horn emphasize in Paragraph 5? The necessity to stop developers from evading taxes.","霍恩在第五段强调了什么？阻止开发商逃税的必要性。","选项"],["2023 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1 · 第23题 · 选项A","In Paragraph 4, supporters of fake grass point out the necessity to lower the costs of fake grass.","在第四段中，人造草坪的支持者指出，有必要降低人造草坪的成本。","选项"]],"necessity.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neg- = deny, 表示“否认”，原始印欧语形式为 *ne- (no, not)，和词根 un- 同源。"],["词根","ced-,ceed-,cess- = go away; withdraw, yield, 表示“走开，撤退，屈服”。来自拉丁语。"],["后缀","-ary 表形容词，“…的”。"],["后缀","-ity 表名词，指具备某种性质。"]],"d":[]}],"negative":[["ˈneɡ.ə.tɪv","ˈneɡ·ə·t̬ɪv"],["CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["复数","negatives"],["原形","negative"],["第三人称单数","negatives"],["现在分词","negativing"],["过去式","negatived"],["过去分词","negatived"],["副词","negatively",1],["名词","negativeness",1],["名词","negativity",1]],[33,4.0,20,15,6],[["adj.","坏的；有害的",15],["adj.","否定的",0],["adj.","消极的；负面的；缺乏热情的",17],["adj.","结果为阴性的（或否定的）",0],["adj.","负极的；阴极的",0],["adj.","负的；小于零的",1],["n.","否定词；否定；拒绝",0],["n.","属阴性（或否定）的结果",0],["n.","含有否定词的；否定的",0],["n.","负片；底片",0],["v.","拒绝；否定",0],["v.","否定…的真实性；证伪",0]],[["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","A great example of this is Europe’s largest supercomputer, LUMI in Finland, which is astonishingly carbon-negative.","一个很好的例子是位于芬兰的欧洲最大超级计算机LUMI，它竟然实现了负碳排放。","正文"],["2023 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","A new study published in the journal Child Development, by Eveline Crone of the University of Leiden and colleagues, suggests that the positive and negative sides of teenagers go hand in hand.","莱顿大学的埃弗莉娜·克罗内及其同事在《儿童发展》杂志发表的一项新研究表明，青少年的积极面和消极面相伴而生。","正文"],["2023 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","The participants filled out questionnaires about how often they did things that were altruistic and positive, like sacrificing their own interests to help a friend, or rebellious and negative, like getting drunk or staying out late.","参与者填写问卷，报告自己做出利他、积极行为（如牺牲个人利益帮助朋友）或叛逆、消极行为（如喝醉酒或深夜不归）的频率。","正文"],["2020 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","One study found that people responded best to comments that shifted from negative to positive, possibly because it suggested they had won somebody over.","一项研究发现，人们对从批评转为赞扬的评价反应最好，或许是因为这让他们觉得自己赢得了某人的认可。","正文"],["2020 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","A more direct finding is that people who scored high for negative emotions like anxiety looked at others for shorter periods of time and reported more comfortable feelings when others did not look directly at them.","一项更直接的发现是：焦虑等负面情绪得分较高的人注视他人的时间较短，而且在别人不直视自己时，他们报告说感觉更自在。","正文"],["2019 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Using caregiver assessments and the children's self-observations, she rated each child's overall sympathy level and his or her tendency to feel negative emotions after moral transgressions.","她根据照料者的评估和孩子们的自我观察，评定了每个孩子的总体同情心水平，以及他们在道德越轨后产生负面情绪的倾向。","正文"]],"negative.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neg- = deny, 表示“否认”，原始印欧语形式为 *ne- (no, not)，和词根 un- 同源。"],["后缀","-ate 表动词，“做，造成”。"],["后缀","-ive,-ative,-itive 表形容词。"]],"d":[["seronegative","阴性"],["binegative","二阴电荷的"],["negatively","负"],["negativism","n. 否定论,消极论,反对癖性"],["negativist","否定"]]}],"negotiate":[["nəˈɡəʊ.ʃi.eɪt","nɪˈɡoʊ·ʃiˌeɪt"],["高中","CET6","考研","TOEFL","GRE"],[["原形","negotiate"],["第三人称单数","negotiates"],["现在分词","negotiating"],["过去式","negotiated"],["过去分词","negotiated"],["名词","negotiator",1],["形容词","negotiatory",1],["名词","negotiation",1]],[8,2.5,3,7,0],[["v.","谈判；磋商；协商",4],["v.","商定，达成（协议）",4],["v.","通过，越过（险要路段）",0]],[["2016 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Negotiated by USFWS and the states, the plan requires individuals and businesses that damage habitat as part of their operations to pay into a fund to replace every acre destroyed with 2 new acres of suitable habitat.","这项由该局和各州协商制定的计划要求：因经营活动破坏栖息地的个人和企业，须向一项基金缴款，用新建的两英亩适宜栖息地来替代每一英亩被破坏的栖息地。","正文"],["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","Either way, one benefit of “a national” organization would be to negotiate better prices, if possible, with drug manufacturers.","无论采用哪种形式，“全国性”机构的一个好处是，有可能与制药企业谈出更好的价格。","正文"],["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","Rather than, say, Quebec, negotiating on behalf of seven million people, the national agency would negotiate on behalf of 31 million people.","举例说，谈判不再由魁北克代表七百万人进行，而是由全国性机构代表三千一百万人进行。","正文"],["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","Instead of having one province — or a series of hospitals within a province — negotiate a price for a given drug on the provincial list, the national agency would negotiate on behalf of all provinces.","全国性机构可以代表所有省份协商价格，而不必由某个省，或省内的一系列医院，分别就省级清单上的某种药品谈价。","正文"],["2004 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Some use them to keep a close watch on the demand for their line of work or gather information on compensation to arm themselves when negotiating for a raise.","有些人用它们密切关注自己行业的用人需求，或搜集薪酬信息，以便在谈加薪时更有底气。","正文"],["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part B · 选项B","B) Or they could read Mr. Kirby’s report: “The substantial buying power of such an agency would strengthen the public prescription-drug insurance plans to negotiate the lowest possible purchase prices from drug companies.”","B）或者他们可以读读柯比先生的报告：“这样一个机构强大的购买力将增强公共处方药保险计划与制药公司谈判的能力，以争取尽可能低的采购价格。”",""]],"negotiate.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neg- = deny, 表示“否认”，原始印欧语形式为 *ne- (no, not)，和词根 un- 同源。"],["词根","oti- 表示“休闲”。"],["后缀","-ate 表动词，“做，造成”。"]],"d":[["negotiator","n. 磋商者;交涉者 出售者;交易者;转让者"],["negotiation","n. 协商, 谈判 完成(难事);通过"],["renegotiate","重新谈判"]]}],"narrative":[["ˈnær.ə.tɪv","ˈnær·ə·t̬ɪv"],["CET6","考研","IELTS","GRE"],[["复数","narratives"],["副词","narratively",1]],[7,2.0,5,4,0],[["n.","（尤指小说中的）描述，叙述",2],["adj.","讲故事；叙述；叙事技巧",2],["n.","体现一套目标或价值观的事件解释方式；叙事说法",3]],[["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","“Such narratives can lead to maternal exhaustion and have dangerous consequences,” they wrote.","他们写道：“这类观念会使母亲精疲力竭，并产生危险的后果。”","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","This abrupt shift to an “intensive mothering narrative”, which suggests that mothers should manage childcare alone, was likely to have been harmful.","这种向“密集母职”观念的突然转变，很可能造成了伤害；这种观念认为母亲应独自承担育儿责任。","正文"],["2023 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","By allowing AI to develop content some brand marketers may find that they are losing control over the brand narrative.","如果让人工智能开发内容，一些品牌营销人员可能会发现自己正在失去对品牌叙事的控制。","正文"],["2001 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","In other words, there is a conventional story line in the newsroom culture that provides a backbone and a ready-made narrative structure for otherwise confusing news.","换言之，新闻编辑室文化中存在一套惯用的叙事模式，为原本纷繁难解的新闻提供主线和现成的叙事结构。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part B · 选项H","You don’t need technology for an immersive experience — just surrender to narratives across time and place.","获得沉浸式体验不需要技术；只要投入到跨越时空的故事中即可。",""],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2 · 第28题 · 选项D","According to Paragraph 4, the “intensive mothering narrative” departs from the course of evolution.","根据第四段，“密集母职”这一观念背离了进化的历程。","题干"]],"narrative.mp3",{"r":[["后缀","-ate 表动词，“做，造成”。"],["词根","gn-,gnos-,gnor- = know, 表示“知道”，来自拉丁语。"],["后缀","-ive,-ative,-itive 表形容词。"]],"d":[]}],"narrow":[["ˈnær.əʊ","ˈnær·oʊ"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL"],[["复数","narrows"],["原形","narrow"],["第三人称单数","narrows"],["现在分词","narrowing"],["过去式","narrowed"],["过去分词","narrowed"],["比较级","narrower"],["最高级","narrowest"],["副词","narrowly",1],["名词","narrowness",1]],[13,3.0,9,10,2],[["adj.","狭窄的；窄小的",0],["adj.","勉强的；刚刚好的",1],["adj.","（种类或数目）有限的；范围小的",3],["adj.","狭隘的；目光短浅的",0],["adj.","狭义的；严格的；准确的",0],["v.","使窄小；变窄；缩小",9]],[["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","But understanding where the animals were first domesticated could guide archaeologists to a narrow region to search for insights about the original tamed donkeys.","不过，弄清这些动物最初在哪里被驯化，可以帮助考古学家缩小寻找范围，以发掘有关最早驯养的驴的线索。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","This narrowing of the regulatory scope was a victory for builders, mining operators and other commercial interests often at odds with environmental rules.","监管范围的收窄是建筑商、采矿业者及其他常与环保规定相抵触的商业利益方的一场胜利。","正文"],["2015 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","They cite past research by several authors to show that this is the gap that must be narrowed to close the achievement gap.","他们引用几位作者此前的研究，说明必须缩小的是这一差距，才能弥合成就差距。","正文"],["2010 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","The Federal Circuit’s action comes in the wake of a series of recent decisions by the Supreme Court that has narrowed the scope of protections for patent holders.","联邦巡回上诉法院是在最高法院最近作出一系列缩小专利持有人保护范围的裁决之后采取这一行动的。","正文"],["2008 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","The three-fifths formula handed Jefferson his narrow victory in the presidential election of 1800 by inflating the votes of the southern states in the Electoral College.","五分之三折算法抬高了南方各州在选举人团中的票数，使杰斐逊在1800年总统选举中险胜。","正文"],["2004 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","For any job search, you should start with a narrow concept — what you think you want to do — then broaden it.","找任何工作时，你都应该先确定一个较窄的目标——你认为自己想做什么——然后再扩大范围。","正文"]],"narrow.mp3",null],"nasty":[["ˈnɑː.sti","ˈnæs·ti"],["CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[["比较级","nastier"],["最高级","nastiest"],["副词","nastily",1],["名词","nastiness",1]],[5,2.0,5,4,0],[["adj.","极差的；令人厌恶的；令人不悦的",3],["adj.","不友好的；恶意的；令人不愉快的",1],["adj.","危险的；严重的",1],["adj.","无礼的；污秽的；下流的",0]],[["2019 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Some kids who are low in sympathy may make up for that shortfall by experiencing more guilt, which can rein in their nastier impulses.","一些同情心较弱的孩子，可能因感到更多内疚而弥补这一不足，这种内疚感能约束他们那些较恶劣的冲动。","正文"],["2017 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","The court did suggest that accepting favors in return for opening doors is “distasteful” and “nasty.”","法院确实表示，以帮人疏通关系来换取好处的行为“令人反感”且“卑劣”。","正文"],["2007 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Just as bosses and boards have finally sorted out their worst accounting and compliance troubles, and improved their feeble corporation governance, a new problem threatens to earn them — especially in America — the sort of nasty headlines that inevitably lead to heads rolling in the executive suite: data insecurity.","就在公司高管和董事会终于理清最棘手的会计与合规问题，并改善薄弱的公司治理之时，一个新问题又可能让他们——尤其是美国的高管——登上令人难堪的新闻头条，而这种头条免不了导致管理层有人丢掉职位：数据缺乏安全保障。","正文"],["2002 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Since the dawn of human ingenuity, people have devised ever more cunning tools to cope with work that is dangerous, boring, burdensome, or just plain nasty.","自人类开始展现聪明才智以来，人们就不断设计出越来越巧妙的工具，来应付危险、枯燥、繁重或纯粹令人厌恶的工作。","正文"],["2008 英一 · 完形","They also suffer more often than most people from a number of nasty genetic diseases, such as breast cancer.","他们患上多种严重遗传病的频率也高于多数人，比如乳腺癌。",""]],"nasty.mp3",null],"nation":[["ˈneɪ.ʃᵊn","ˈneɪ·ʃən"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研"],[["复数","nations"],["形容词","nationless",1],["形容词","national",1],["副词","nationally",1]],[36,4.0,21,23,1],[["n.","国家；民族",29],["n.","国民",7]],[["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","This must begin with the question of how we maximise the health of the nation, rather than “fix” the NHS.","讨论必须从如何最大限度改善全国人民的健康状况出发，而不是从如何“修复”国民保健署出发。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","I would ask that the foreign nations and the original country discuss the terms of transfer.","我希望外国与原属国商讨移交条件。","正文"],["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","The performance was a creative call to action ahead of November’s United Nations Climate Change Conference in Glasgow, UK.","这场演出是在当年11月英国格拉斯哥举行的联合国气候变化大会之前，发出的一次富有创意的行动呼吁。","正文"],["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","Oman rated Scovell’s significance highly, but at the same time, the general nature of his History meant that (48) he could not analyze carefully what this obscure officer may or may not have contributed to that great struggle between nations or indeed tell us anything much about the man himself.","奥曼高度评价斯科维尔的重要性；但与此同时，《半岛战争史》的通史性质意味着，他无法仔细分析这名默默无闻的军官究竟对那场国家间的大战作出了什么贡献（如果确有贡献的话），更无法向我们详细介绍其本人。","正文"],["2021 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","A move back to self-sufficiency, the argument goes, would boost the farming industry, political sovereignty and even the nation’s health.","支持者称，恢复食品自给自足会促进农业、增强政治主权，甚至有益于国民健康。","正文"],["2020 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","France’s planned tax is a clear warning: Unless a broad consensus can be reached on reforming the international tax system, other nations are likely to follow suit, and American companies will face a cascade of different taxes from dozens of nations that will prove burdensome and costly.","法国计划征收的税发出了明确警告：除非各方就改革国际税收体系达成广泛共识，否则其他国家很可能效仿；届时美国公司将面对数十个国家接连征收的不同税种，负担沉重且代价高昂。","正文"]],"nation.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nat-,nai- = born, 表示“出生的”，来自古典拉丁语 gnasci，由词根 gen-（出生，产生）组成。"],["后缀","-ion,-ation,-ition 表名词，“行为、动作、状态、过程、结果；物品”等。"]],"d":[["international","adj. 国际的, 国际间进行的"],["national","1. adj. 国家的；国民的；民族的；国立的 2. n. 国民"],["multinational","跨国公司"],["transnational","adj. 影响数国的;数国参与的;跨国的"],["supranational","adj. 超国家的；超民族的"]]}],"national":[["ˈnæʃ.ᵊn.ᵊl","ˈnæʃ·ə·nᵊl"],["中考","高中","CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[["复数","nationals"],["副词","nationally",1]],[92,5.0,28,60,6],[["adj.","国家的；民族的；全国的",91],["adj.","国有的；国立的；国营的",1],["n.","（某国的）公民",0]],[["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Between two great wars this technological innovation built a new kind of national consciousness.","在两次大战之间，这项技术创新塑造了一种新的国民共同意识。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","At Yosemite National Park, Martin oversaw the use of what is known as prescribed burns to make the landscape more resilient.","在优胜美地国家公园，马丁曾监督开展所谓的“计划烧除”，以增强当地生态环境的韧性。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Ferrovie dello Stato Italiane, the publicly controlled group that owns train operator Trenitalia and the national train network RFI, said 23 percent of all high-speed trains it operated were late in 2023.","意大利国家铁路集团是一家受政府控制的集团，旗下拥有铁路运营商意大利铁路公司和全国铁路网运营商 RFI；该集团表示，2023 年其运营的高铁列车有 23% 晚点。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","(49) It wasn’t until the phrase “scientific literacy” came along in the 1940s that science had the formidable slogan it needed to command public attention and make improving science education an important national goal.","（49）直到20世纪40年代“科学素养”一词出现，科学才有了它所需要的有力口号，可以借此吸引公众关注，并使改进科学教育成为重要的国家目标。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","The review recommends a national branding campaign to give libraries a stronger physical presence, the reintroduction of a scheme to enable members to use their card in any library in the country, and automatic memberships for children.","评估报告建议开展全国性的品牌宣传活动，提升图书馆实体场所的公众可见度；恢复一项让读者凭会员卡使用全国任何一家图书馆的制度；并让儿童自动获得会员资格。","正文"],["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","That day’s high temperature of roughly 36°C was 1°C shy of the heat wave alert threshold for coastal cities set by national meteorological authorities.","当天约 36 摄氏度的最高气温，比国家气象部门为沿海城市设定的热浪预警阈值低 1 摄氏度。","正文"]],"national.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nat-,nai- = born, 表示“出生的”，来自古典拉丁语 gnasci，由词根 gen-（出生，产生）组成。"],["后缀","-ion,-ation,-ition 表名词，“行为、动作、状态、过程、结果；物品”等。"],["后缀","-al,-ial 表形容词，“…的”，一般缀于名词后。"]],"d":[["nationality","n. 国籍 民族群体"],["nationally","全国"],["nationalise","收归国有"],["nationalism","民族主义"],["nationalist","民族主义者"]]}],"nationality":[["ˌnæʃ.ᵊnˈæl.ə.ti","ˌnæʃ·əˈnæl·ɪ·t̬i"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["复数","nationalities"]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["n.","国籍",1],["n.","（构成国家一部分的）民族",0]],[["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","Anyone can be a citizen scientist, regardless of age, nationality or academic experience.","任何人都可以成为公民科学家，无论年龄、国籍或学术经历如何。","正文"]],"nationality.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nat-,nai- = born, 表示“出生的”，来自古典拉丁语 gnasci，由词根 gen-（出生，产生）组成。"],["后缀","-ion,-ation,-ition 表名词，“行为、动作、状态、过程、结果；物品”等。"],["后缀","-al,-ial 表形容词，“…的”，一般缀于名词后。"],["后缀","-ity 表名词，指具备某种性质。"]],"d":[]}],"native":[["ˈneɪ.tɪv","ˈneɪ·t̬ɪv"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[["复数","natives"],["副词","natively",1],["名词","nativeness",1]],[17,3.0,10,13,1],[["adj.","出生地的；儿时居住地的",4],["adj.","本地的；当地的",1],["adj.","土著的；土著人的",4],["adj.","原产于某地的；土产的；当地的",4],["adj.","天赋的；与生俱来的",3],["n.","出生于某国（或某地）的人",0],["n.","本地人；当地人",0],["n.","（旧时欧洲人用以称呼先于白人居住在某地的人）土著",0],["n.","本地的动物（或植物）",0],["n.","数字土著，数字原住民（因与数码技术、电脑等一起成长而对此非常熟悉的人）",1]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","Asia is arguably the region most neglected by global efforts to increase diversity in restoration and to study native species.","在全球增加生态恢复多样性、研究本地物种的努力中，亚洲或许是最受忽视的地区。","正文"],["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","The Wickquasgeck Trail is an example of a historical desire path, created by Native Americans to cross the forests of Manhattan and move between settlements quickly.","威克夸斯格克小径是一条历史上的愿望路径，由美洲原住民开辟，供他们穿越曼哈顿的森林，在定居点之间快速往来。","正文"],["2024 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","While productive tree planting can deliver real financial benefits to rural economies and contribute to the UK’s net-zero strategy, the focus of government support continues to be on food production and the rewilding and planting of native woodland solely for biodiversity.","尽管为生产木材而植树能给农村经济带来实实在在的经济利益，并有助于英国的净零排放战略，但政府的支持仍集中在粮食生产，以及仅以生物多样性为目的的生态恢复和本土林地种植上。","正文"],["2019 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","One oft-debated cure for this labor shortage remains as implausible as it's been all along: Native U.S. workers won't be returning to the farm.","针对这一劳动力短缺问题，一种经常被讨论的解决办法始终不切实际：美国本土工人不会重返农场。","正文"],["2018 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Young people who are digital natives are indeed becoming more skillful at separating fact from fiction in cyberspace.","在数字时代长大的年轻人确实越来越善于在网络空间辨别真假。","正文"],["2018 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","(49) A native literary drama had been created, its alliance with the public playhouses established, and at least some of its great traditions had been begun.","（49）本土文学戏剧由此诞生，与公共剧院的联盟得到确立，其重要传统中至少有一些也已开始形成。","正文"]],"native.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nat-,nai- = born, 表示“出生的”，来自古典拉丁语 gnasci，由词根 gen-（出生，产生）组成。"],["后缀","-ive 表名词后缀，“人或物”。"]],"d":[["nativity","n. 出生；出生地；（Nativity）耶稣的诞生"],["natively","adv. 天然地；生来地"],["nativism","n. 先天论；本土主义"],["nativist","n. 先天论者；本土主义者；本土文化保护者"],["native-born","土生土长的"]]}],"natural":[["ˈnætʃ.ᵊr.ᵊl","ˈnætʃ·ər·əl"],["中考","高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["复数","naturals"],["名词","naturalness",1],["副词","naturally",1]],[48,4.0,26,31,4],[["adj.","自然的；天然的",34],["adj.","天赋的；天生具有某种能力的",1],["adj.","正常的；自然的；意料之中的",9],["adj.","天生的；本能的；与生俱来的",3],["adj.","不拘束的；不做作的；自然的",1],["adj.","有血缘关系的；亲生的",0],["adj.","非婚生的；私生的",0],["adj.","符合人的理性的；正常的；自然的",0],["adj.","本位音的，标有还原号的（书写符号为 ♮）",0],["n.","有天赋的人；擅长做某事的人",0],["n.","本位音，还原音，本位号（书写符号为 ♮）",0]],[["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","(47) But by utilising the natural curiosity of the general public it is possible to overcome many of these challenges by engaging non-scientists directly in the research process.","（47）但是，利用普通公众天生的好奇心，让非科学家直接参与研究过程，就有可能克服其中许多挑战。","正文"],["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Often appearing as trodden dirt tracks through otherwise neat green spaces, these routes of collective disobedience cut corners, bisect lawns and cross hills, representing the natural capability of people (and animals) to go from point A to point B most effectively.","这些集体“违规”开辟的路线通常是在原本整齐的绿地上踩出的小土路：它们抄近道、斜穿草坪、越过山丘，体现出人（和动物）以最高效率从甲地到乙地的天性。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","The miracle of the Chesapeake Bay lies not in its depths, but in the complexity of its natural construction, the interaction of fresh and saline waters, and the mix of land and water.","切萨皮克湾的奇妙之处不在于水深，而在于自然构造的复杂性、淡水与咸水的交汇，以及陆地与水域的交错。","正文"],["2023 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","However, supporters of fake grass point out that there is also an environmental impact with natural lawns, which need mowing and therefore usually consume electricity or petrol.","然而，人造草坪的支持者指出，天然草坪同样会影响环境，因为它需要修剪，通常因此要耗用电力或汽油。","正文"],["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","No matter how you “enhance” enclosures, they do not allow for freedom, a natural diet or adequate exercise.","无论你怎样“改善”围栏环境，它们都无法让动物获得自由、天然的食物或足够的运动。","正文"],["2022 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","In barely more than a decade, organic eggs went from being dismissed as a niche product in natural foods stores to being sold at Walmart.","短短十余年，有机鸡蛋从天然食品店里被人看轻的小众商品，变成了沃尔玛货架上的商品。","正文"]],"natural.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nat-,nai- = born, 表示“出生的”，来自古典拉丁语 gnasci，由词根 gen-（出生，产生）组成。"],["后缀","-ture,-ature,-iture 表名词，通常在单词或词根以t结尾时使用，表示“一般状态，行为”。"],["后缀","-al,-ial 表形容词，“…的”，一般缀于名词后。"]],"d":[["naturally","adv. 天然地; 天生地 自然; 当然 表现自然地, 不做作地"],["supernatural","adj. 超自然的;鬼、神或幻术所引起的 n. 超自然的事物, 超自然现象"],["naturalise","1. vt. 使入国籍；使归化 2. vi. 加入国籍；归化（等于naturalize）"],["preternatural","adj. 异常的,奇特的 超自然的 不可思议的"],["supernaturalism","超自然"]]}],"nature":[["ˈneɪ.tʃəʳ","ˈneɪ·tʃər"],["中考","高中","CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[["复数","natures"]],[54,4.5,26,32,12],[["n.","自然界；大自然",23],["n.","自然；自然方式",0],["n.","天性；本性；性格",11],["n.","基本特征；本质；基本性质",20],["n.","种类；类型",0],["n.","有…本性的；…性情的",0]],[["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","A Reddit webpage devoted to the phenomenon, boasting nearly 50,000 members, showcases images of local desire paths adorned with signs instructing pedestrians to adhere to designated walkways, underscoring the rebellious nature inherent in these human-made tracks.","Reddit 上一个专门讨论这一现象的页面拥有近五万名成员，展示了各地愿望路径的照片；照片中的标牌要求行人只走指定步道，凸显出这些人踩出来的小路所固有的反叛意味。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","Artifacts in museums have the power to inspire, and perhaps spark that need to learn and understand the nature of their creators.","博物馆里的文物能够启发人，也许还能激起人们学习并理解其创造者特质的愿望。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","The Gutenberg printing press transformed civilisation not by changing the nature of writing but by changing its cost — and it would have achieved little without a parallel collapse in the price of surfaces to write on, thanks to an often-overlooked technology called paper.","古腾堡印刷机改变文明，靠的不是改变书写的性质，而是降低书写的成本；若非纸张这一常被忽视的技术使书写材料的价格也大幅下降，它本来也成不了多少事。","正文"],["2023 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","The national parks provide great value to U.S. residents both as places to escape and as symbols of nature.","国家公园既是人们暂时远离日常生活的去处，也是大自然的象征，因此对美国居民具有很大价值。","正文"],["2023 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Moreover, increased privatization would certainly undercut one of the major reasons why 300 million visitors come to the parks each year: to enjoy nature and get a break from the commercial drumbeat that overwhelms daily life.","此外，扩大私有化必定会损害每年吸引3亿游客前来公园的一大原因：亲近自然，暂时摆脱充斥日常生活的商业喧嚣。","正文"],["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","Our research provides strong support for the value of zoos in connecting people with animals and with nature.","我们的研究有力支持动物园在连接人与动物、人与自然方面具有价值这一观点。","正文"]],"nature.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nat-,nai- = born, 表示“出生的”，来自古典拉丁语 gnasci，由词根 gen-（出生，产生）组成。"],["后缀","-ture,-ature,-iture 表名词，通常在单词或词根以t结尾时使用，表示“一般状态，行为”。"]],"d":[["natural","1. adj. 自然的；不做作的；天生的；物质的 2. n. 白痴；自然的事情；[音]本位音"],["denature","1. vt. 使…失去人性；改变…的性质 2. vi. 变性"],["naturism","n. 对自然现象的崇拜；裸体主义"],["naturist","n. 裸体主义者（指认为裸体有益身心的人）；天体运动者（等于nudist）"],["disnature","v. 使不自然,使失去自然形态"]]}],"noble":[["ˈnəʊ.bᵊl","ˈnoʊ·bəl"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[["复数","nobles"],["比较级","nobler"],["最高级","noblest"],["名词","nobleness",1],["副词","nobly",1],["形容词","unnoble",1]],[5,2.0,5,3,1],[["adj.","崇高的；品质高尚的",4],["adj.","贵族的；高贵的",1],["adj.","宏伟的；壮丽的",0],["n.","出身高贵的人；贵族成员",0]],[["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","She uses outdated research and decades-old examples to undermine the noble mission of organizations committed to connecting children to a world beyond their own.","她借助过时的研究和几十年前的事例，贬损那些致力于帮助儿童认识自身世界之外的天地的机构所肩负的崇高使命。","正文"],["2012 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","“The valuable examples which they furnish of the power of self-help, of patient purpose, resolute working, and steadfast integrity, issuing in the formation of truly noble and manly character, exhibit,” wrote Smiles, “what it is in the power of each to accomplish for himself.”","斯迈尔斯写道：“他们留下的宝贵榜样，展示了自助的力量、对目标的持久坚守、果敢实干和始终如一的正直，从而形成真正高尚、刚毅的品格，也展示了每个人靠自己能够取得怎样的成就。”","正文"],["2004 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Practicality, common sense, and native intelligence have been considered more noble qualities than anything you could learn from a book.","实用性、常识和天生的聪明才智，一向被看作比从书本上学到的任何东西更高尚的品质。","正文"],["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4 · 第40题 · 选项D","According to the last paragraph, “paper plates” is to “china” as “humble” is to “noble”.","根据最后一段，“纸盘”与“瓷盘”的关系，就如同“卑微”与“高贵”的关系。","选项"],["2001 英一 · 写作 · 第46题","Among all the worthy feelings of mankind, love is probably the noblest, but everyone has his/her own understanding of it.","在人类所有美好的感情中，爱或许是最高尚的，但每个人对爱的理解各不相同。",""]],"noble.mp3",{"r":[["词根","gn-,gnos-,gnor- = know, 表示“知道”，来自拉丁语。"]],"d":[["ennoble","vt. 使…成为贵族；使…高贵；授予爵位"],["nobly","adv. 崇高地；高贵地；华丽地；豪爽地"],["nobility","n. 贵族；高尚；高贵"],["nobleman","n. 贵族"],["nobiliary","贵族的"]]}],"norm":[["nɔːm","nɔrm"],["CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS","GRE"],[["复数","norms"],["形容词","normal",1],["名词","normality",1],["副词","normally",1]],[14,3.0,11,11,1],[["n.","常态；正常行为",6],["n.","规范；行为标准",8],["n.","标准；定额；定量",0],["v.","规范；规定",0]],[["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Today’s tip requests are often not connected to the salary and service norms that used to determine when and how people tip.","如今，索要小费往往与过去决定人们何时及如何付小费的工资和服务惯例无关。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Kung children as young as four will help to look after younger ones and “baby-wearing”, in which infants are carried in slings, is considered the norm.","昆族儿童年仅四岁就会帮忙照看更小的孩子；用背带携带婴儿的“背婴”也被视为常态。","正文"],["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","But they are the exception, not the norm that Ms. Marris implies.","但那只是例外，而非马里斯女士暗示的常态。","正文"],["2021 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","The thought of holding a fixed grin as the camera performed its magical duties was too much to contemplate, and so a non-committal blank stare became the norm.","想到要在相机施展魔法的整个过程中一直咧嘴笑着，实在让人难以接受；于是，不表露情绪的空洞目光成了常态。","正文"],["2021 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","When a faculty or department grows from, say, five to 20 members within three or four years, (49) and when the new staff are predominantly young men and women fresh from postgraduate study, they largely define the norms of academic life in that faculty.","当一个学院或系在三四年内从比如说五名教员增加到二十名时，（49）如果新教员又主要是刚完成研究生学业的年轻男女，那么他们就会在很大程度上决定该学院的学术生活规范。","正文"],["2019 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Unlike so-called basic emotions such as sadness, fear, and anger, guilt emerges a little later, in conjunction with a child's growing grasp of social and moral norms.","与悲伤、恐惧和愤怒等所谓的基本情绪不同，内疚感出现得稍晚一些，与儿童对社会和道德规范日益深入的理解相伴而生。","正文"]],"norm.mp3",{"r":[["词根","norm- = rule, norm, 表示“规则，规范”，来自拉丁语。"]],"d":[]}],"normal":[["ˈnɔː.məl","ˈnɔr·məl"],["中考","高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["复数","normals"],["名词","normality",1],["副词","normally",1]],[12,2.5,8,8,0],[["adj.","典型的；正常的；一般的",12],["adj.","精神正常的；意识健全的",0],["n.","常态；通常标准；一般水平",0],["n.","典型的；正常的；一般的",0]],[["2017 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","In it, a mother is asked to interact with her child in a normal way before putting on a blank expression and not giving them any visual social feedback: the child becomes increasingly distressed as she tries to capture her mother’s attention.","在这个实验中，母亲先被要求正常地与孩子互动，然后摆出一副面无表情的样子，不给孩子任何可见的社交反馈；孩子越想引起母亲注意，就越感到痛苦。","正文"],["2016 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Breaking down problems into bite-sized chunks and using code to solve them becomes normal.","把问题拆解成便于处理的小块，再用代码解决，对他们来说会成为常态。","正文"],["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","But keeping sensitive information on these devices is increasingly a requirement of normal life.","但在这些设备上保存敏感信息，正日益成为正常生活的必需。","正文"],["2015 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","This normal human reaction is used to protect us by signaling danger and preparing us to deal with it.","这种正常的人类反应通过提示危险并让我们准备应对危险来保护我们。","正文"],["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","In today’s world, it has become normal that well-paid executives should not be accountable for what happens in the organisations that they run.","在当今世界，高薪高管不对自己所管理机构发生的事负责，已经成了常态。","正文"],["2003 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Death is normal; we are genetically programmed to disintegrate and perish, even under ideal conditions.","死亡是正常的；即使在理想条件下，基因也决定了我们终会衰败、死亡。","正文"]],"normal.mp3",{"r":[["词根","norm- = rule, norm, 表示“规则，规范”，来自拉丁语。"],["后缀","-al,-ial 表形容词，“…的”，一般缀于名词后。"]],"d":[["abnormal","adj. 反常的，不规则的；变态的"],["normally","adv. 正常地；通常地，一般地"],["paranormal","adj. 超常的；超过正常范围的"],["subnormal","低于正常"],["supernormal","adj. 非凡的,异于寻常的"]]}],"normalization":[["ˌnɔː.məˌlaɪˈzeɪ.ʃn̩","ˌnɔr·mə·ləˈzeɪ·ʃən"],["CET6","考研"],[["复数","normalizations"]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","使符合正常模式或状态的过程；恢复正常的过程；正常化",0]],[],"normalization.mp3",{"r":[["词根","norm- = rule, norm, 表示“规则，规范”，来自拉丁语。"],["后缀","-al,-ial 表形容词，“…的”，一般缀于名词后。"],["后缀","-ise, -ize 动词后缀，一般缀于形容词后。-ise 是英式英语，-ize 是美式英语。"],["后缀","-ion,-ation,-ition 表名词，“行为、动作、状态、过程、结果；物品”等。"]],"d":[["prenormalization","n. 预规格化"]]}],"note":[["nəʊt","noʊt"],["中考","高中","TOEFL"],[["复数","notes"],["原形","note"],["第三人称单数","notes"],["现在分词","noting"],["过去式","noted"],["过去分词","noted"],["名词","noter",1]],[42,4.0,26,30,0],[["n.","笔记；记录",4],["n.","短笺；便条",0],["n.","（听讲或读书等时的）记录，笔记",0],["n.","（有关演出、演员经历、音乐等的）图书资料，录音或唱片等封套介绍",0],["n.","注释；按语；批注",1],["n.","纸币",0],["n.","单音；音调；音符",0],["n.","特征；口气；调子；气氛",2],["n.","正式文件；票据；证明书",0],["n.","（外交文书）照会；通牒",0],["v.","注意；留意",3],["v.","指出；特别提到",30],["v.","笔记；记录",0],["n.","重要的；引人注目的",1],["n.","注意到；将…铭记在心",1]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Employers are taking note and taking action.","雇主们已经注意到了这一点，并开始采取行动。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","Much of the global funding for restoration is dedicated to developing it as a tool to mitigate climate change, notes restoration ecologist Pedro Brancalion.","恢复生态学家佩德罗·布兰卡利翁指出，全球用于生态恢复的大部分资金，都致力于将其发展成缓解气候变化的工具。","正文"],["2022 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","And if real, she notes, it might be reversible by another nudge: “Easy come, easy go.”","她指出，如果效果真实存在，也可能被另一次轻微干预逆转：“来得容易，去得也快。”","正文"],["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","Studying Scovell’s papers at the Public Record Office, London, I found that he had left an extensive journal and copious notes about his work in the Peninsula.","在伦敦公共档案馆研究斯科维尔的文件时，我发现他留下了内容丰富的日记，以及大量关于自己在半岛工作的笔记。","正文"],["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Fewer artist than scientists responded to the Nature poll; however, several respondents noted that artists do not simply assist scientists with their communication requirements.","参加《自然》杂志调查的艺术家少于科学家；不过，几位受访者指出，艺术家并非只是帮助科学家满足传播需求。","正文"],["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Joana Lia Ferreira, an assistant professor of conservation and restoration at the NOVA School of Science and Technology, notes that archaeologists first defined the great material ages of human history — Stone Age, Iron Age, and so on — after examining artifacts in museums.","诺瓦科学技术学院文物保护与修复专业助理教授若阿娜·莉娅·费雷拉指出，考古学家正是在研究博物馆藏品后，才首次划分出人类历史上的重要物质时代，如石器时代、铁器时代等。","正文"]],"note.mp3",{"r":[["词根","not- = know, 表示“知道，注意”，和表示知道的词根 gn- 同源。"]],"d":[["notebook","n. 笔记本，笔记簿；手册"],["noted","1. adj. 著名的；显著的；[音]附有乐谱的 2. v. 注意；记下（note的过去式和过去分词）"],["notary","n. 公证人"],["noter","n. 做笔记者；摘记者"],["endnote","n. 尾注"]]}],"notion":[["ˈnəʊ.ʃᵊn","ˈnoʊ·ʃən"],["CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["复数","notions"],["形容词","notionless",1],["形容词","notional",1],["名词","notionality",1],["副词","notionally",1]],[9,2.5,8,7,1],[["n.","观念；信念；理解",9]],[["2020 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","“Eye contact and smiles” can signal availability and confidence, a common-sense notion supported in studies by psychologist Monica Moore.","“目光接触和微笑”可以传达愿意交往与自信；这种符合常识的看法得到了心理学家莫妮卡·摩尔的研究支持。","正文"],["2016 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Even better would be to help elevate notions of beauty beyond the material standards of a particular industry.","更好的是，帮助人们将对美的认识提升到某个特定行业的物质标准之上。","正文"],["2014 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","It’s time to reinvent the formula for how work is conducted, since we are still relying on a very 20th century notion of work, Hagel says.","哈格尔说，现在该重新设计工作开展的方式了，因为我们仍然依赖一种十分典型的20世纪工作观。","正文"],["2007 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","For example, notions of evidence and fact, of basic rights and public interest are at work in the process of journalistic judgment and production just as in courts of law.","例如，证据与事实、基本权利与公共利益等概念，不仅在法庭上发挥作用，也贯穿于新闻判断和制作的过程。","正文"],["2007 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","(50) While comment and reaction from lawyers may enhance stories, it is preferable for journalists to rely on their own notions of significance and make their own judgments.","（50）虽然律师的评论和回应可能丰富报道，但记者最好依据自己对事件重要性的认识，独立作出判断。","正文"],["2006 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","The notion is that people have failed to detect the massive changes which have happened in the ocean because they have been looking back only a relatively short time into the past.","这一观点认为，人们之所以未能察觉海洋中发生的巨大变化，是因为他们只往过去回看了相对较短的一段时间。","正文"]],"notion.mp3",{"r":[["词根","not- = know, 表示“知道，注意”，和表示知道的词根 gn- 同源。"],["后缀","-ion,-ation,-ition 表名词，“行为、动作、状态、过程、结果；物品”等。"]],"d":[["notional","adj. 想像的；概念性的；抽象的；不切实际的"]]}],"nerve":[["nɜːv","nɜrv"],["CET4","CET6","考研","GRE"],[["复数","nerves"],["原形","nerve"],["第三人称单数","nerves"],["现在分词","nerving"],["过去式","nerved"],["过去分词","nerved"]],[2,1.0,2,2,0],[["n.","神经",1],["n.","神经质；神经紧张",0],["n.","勇气；气魄",0],["n.","鲁莽；冒失；厚颜",1],["v.","鼓足勇气；振作精神",0]],[["2011 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Some papers even had the nerve to refuse delivery to distant suburbs.","有些报纸甚至敢于拒绝向偏远郊区送报。","正文"],["2002 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","What they found, in attempting to model thought, is that the human brain’s roughly one hundred billion nerve cells are much more talented — and human perception far more complicated — than previously imagined.","他们在尝试模拟思维时发现，人脑中大约一千亿个神经细胞的能力远比先前想象的强，而人的感知也远比先前想象的复杂。","正文"]],"nerve.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neur-,nerv- = nerve 神经，勇气"]],"d":[["nervous","adj. 神经的；紧张不安的；强健有力的"],["nervy","adj. 有勇气的；易激动的；紧张不安的"],["nerves","1. n. 神经；神经紧张；胆量（nerve的复数） 2. v. 使振作；鼓足勇气（nerve的第三人称单数）"],["nerveless","adj. 无力的;无勇气的 沉着的,镇静的"],["nerve-tire","神经衰弱"]]}],"nervous":[["ˈnɜː.vəs","ˈnɜr·vəs"],["中考","高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["副词","nervously",1],["名词","nervousness",1]],[7,2.0,5,4,0],[["adj.","焦虑的；担忧的；惶恐的",2],["adj.","神经质的；易紧张焦虑的；胆怯的",0],["adj.","神经系统的",5]],[["2011 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","In the third quarter, CEO turnover was down 23% from a year ago as nervous boards stuck with the leaders they had, according to Liberum Research.","据利伯伦研究公司称，第三季度首席执行官的更替数量同比下降了23%，因为忧心忡忡的董事会继续留用现有领导者。","正文"],["2008 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","Good writing most often occurs when you are in hot pursuit of an idea rather than in a nervous search for errors.","好文章往往诞生于你热切追寻一个想法的时候，而不是焦虑地搜寻错误的时候。","正文"],["2001 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","Direct links between the brain’s nervous system and a computer will also create full sensory virtual environments, allowing virtual vacations like those in the film Total Recall.","人脑神经系统与计算机之间的直接连接还将创造全感官虚拟环境，使人们能够享受《全面回忆》中那样的虚拟假期。","正文"],["2001 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","“By linking directly to our nervous system, computers could pick up what we feel and, hopefully, simulate feeling too so that we can start to develop full sensory environments, rather like the holidays in Total Recall or the Star Trek holodeck,” he says.","他说：“计算机若与我们的神经系统直接连接，就能感知我们的感觉，并有望模拟感觉。这样，我们便可以开始开发全感官环境，颇像《全面回忆》里的度假体验，或《星际迷航》中的全息甲板。”","正文"],["2022 英一 · 完形","“Since plants don’t have nervous systems, the chances that they have consciousness are effectively zero.”","“由于植物没有神经系统，它们具有意识的可能性实际上为零。”",""],["2022 英一 · 完形","Beginning in 2006, some scientists have argued that plants possess neuron-like cells that interact with hormones and neurotransmitters, forming “a plant nervous system, analogous to that in animals,” said lead study author Lincoln Taiz, “They even claimed that plants have ‘brain-like command centers’ at their root tips.”","研究论文的主要作者林肯·泰兹说，从2006年起，一些科学家就认为，植物拥有类似神经元的细胞，这些细胞与激素和神经递质相互作用，形成“类似于动物神经系统的植物神经系统”。“他们甚至声称，植物的根尖有‘类似大脑的指挥中心’。”",""]],"nervous.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neur-,nerv- = nerve 神经，勇气"],["后缀","-ous,-itious,-eous,-ious,-uous 表形容词，表示“…的”，用于化学领域表示“亚酸的，低价（金属）的”。"]],"d":[["nervousness","n. 神经质,焦躁,胆小"]]}],"nevertheless":[["ˌnev.ə.ðəˈles","ˌnev·ər·ðəˈles"],["CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[],[5,2.0,4,5,0],[["adv.","尽管如此；不过；然而",5]],[["2014 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Nevertheless, the affordable housing situation is desperate.","然而，可负担住房的状况已十分严峻。","正文"],["2011 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","Nevertheless, as any biographer knows, a person's early life and its conditions are often the greatest gift to an individual.","尽管如此，任何传记作者都知道，一个人的早年生活及其境遇，往往是他得到的最珍贵的礼物。","正文"],["2006 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Nevertheless every hotel in town seems to be adding a new wing or cocktail lounge.","然而，镇上似乎家家旅馆都在增建新楼或鸡尾酒吧。","正文"],["2006 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","Nevertheless, Williams’s suit charges that the casino, knowing he was “helplessly addicted to gambling,” intentionally worked to “lure” him to “engage in conduct against his will.”","然而，威廉姆斯在诉状中声称，赌场明知他“无力摆脱赌瘾”，仍有意“引诱”他“从事违背自己意愿的行为”。","正文"],["2001 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Nevertheless, the word “amateur” does carry a connotation that the person concerned is not fully integrated into the scientific community and, in particular, may not fully share its values.","不过，“业余研究者”一词确实暗含这样的意思：此人尚未完全融入科学界，尤其可能未能充分认同其价值观。","正文"]],"nevertheless.mp3",{"r":[["后缀","-less 表形容词，“无…的，不…的”，和单词loss同源。"]],"d":[]}],"naval":[["ˈneɪ.vᵊl","ˈneɪ·vəl"],["CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["副词","navally",1]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["adj.","海军的",0],["n.","从含树脂的针叶树、尤其松树取得的制品（如松节油、沥青、松香）。",1]],[["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","Here was the raw material of houses and furniture, ships and potash, dyes and naval stores.","这里有建造房屋和家具、船只，以及制作钾碱、染料和船舶用品所需的原料。","正文"]],"naval.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nav-,naus-,naut- = ship, 表示“船”，naut- 引申为“海员”。"],["后缀","-al,-ial 表形容词，“…的”，一般缀于名词后。"]],"d":[["navally","adv. 海军地；与海军有关地；船舶地"]]}],"navigation":[["ˌnæv.ɪˈɡeɪ.ʃᵊn","ˌnæv.ɪˈɡeɪ.ʃən"],["CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["复数","navigations"],["形容词","navigational",1],["副词","navigationally",1]],[2,1.0,2,1,0],[["n.","导航；领航",2],["n.","航行",0],["n.","（网站或互联网的）导航",0]],[["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","Although the cues used by African elephants for long-distance navigation are not yet understood, smell may well play a part.","尽管人们尚不了解非洲象远距离导航所依赖的线索，嗅觉很可能起着作用。","正文"],["2019 英一 · 完形","Today, we live in a world where GPS systems, digital maps, and other navigation apps are all available on our smart phones.","如今，GPS系统、数字地图和其他导航应用都能在我们的智能手机上使用。",""]],"navigation.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nav-,naus-,naut- = ship, 表示“船”，naut- 引申为“海员”。"],["词根","ag-,ig-,ass- = do, act, 表示“做，代理做”，来自拉丁语 agere \"actor\" ( 按照预先决定的角色) 行动。"],["后缀","-ate 表动词，“做，造成”。"],["后缀","-ion,-ation,-ition 表名词，“行为、动作、状态、过程、结果；物品”等。"]],"d":[["navigational","adj. 航行的,航海的"],["astronavigation","n. 太空航行"],["radionavigation","无线电导航"],["circumnavigation","n. 世界一周旅行；周游世界"]]}],"navy":[["ˈneɪ.vi","ˈneɪ·vi"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研"],[["复数","navies"]],[6,2.0,2,0,0],[["n.","海军；海军部队",6],["n.","深蓝色",0]],[["2018 英一 · 阅读 · Part B · 选项A","The commission was also to consider possible arrangements for the War and Navy Departments.","该委员会还要考虑陆军部和海军部可能的安置方案。",""],["2018 英一 · 阅读 · Part B · 选项D","It has housed 16 Secretaries of the Navy, 21 Secretaries of War, and 24 Secretaries of State.","这里曾是16位海军部长、21位陆军部长和24位国务卿的办公场所。",""],["2018 英一 · 阅读 · Part B · 选项B","The Navy Department moved into the east wing in 1879, where elaborate wall and ceiling stenciling and marquetry floors decorated the office of the Secretary.","海军部于1879年迁入东翼，部长办公室的墙壁和天花板饰有精美的模板绘图，地面则铺着镶嵌木地板。",""],["2018 英一 · 阅读 · Part B · 选项E","Designed by Supervising Architect of the Treasury, Alfred B. Mullett, it was built from 1871 to 1888 to house the growing staffs of the State, War, and Navy Departments, and is considered one of the best examples of French Second Empire architecture in the country.","这栋大楼由财政部主管建筑师阿尔弗雷德·B.马利特设计，建于1871年至1888年，旨在容纳国务院、陆军部和海军部这三个部门不断扩大的工作人员队伍；它被认为是美国法国第二帝国建筑风格的最佳范例之一。",""],["2018 英一 · 阅读 · Part B · 选项C","C) The State, War, and Navy Building, as it was originally known, housed the three Executive Branch Departments most intimately associated with formulating and conducting the nation’s foreign policy in the last quarter of the nineteenth century and the first quarter of the twentieth century — the period when the United States emerged as an international power.","C）这座建筑最初称为国务院、陆军部和海军部大楼。在19世纪最后25年和20世纪最初25年，也就是美国崛起为国际强国的时期，它容纳了与制定和执行国家外交政策关系最密切的三个行政部门。",""],["2017 英一 · 阅读 · Part B · 选项F","His father was a clerk in the British Navy Pay Office — a respectable position, but with little social status.","他的父亲是英国海军军饷处的一名文员，职位体面，但社会地位并不高。",""]],"navy.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nav-,naus-,naut- = ship, 表示“船”，naut- 引申为“海员”。"],["后缀","-y 表名词，加在形容词或以r结尾的单词后。"]],"d":[["navy-blue","adj. 深蓝色的"]]}],"nearby":[["ˌnɪəˈbaɪ","ˈnɪərˈbɑɪ"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研"],[],[5,2.0,3,3,1],[["adj.","附近的；邻近的",4],["adv.","在附近；不远",1]],[["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Established in an old paper mill, it is powered by a nearby river and its remote heat warms the people who live in the surrounding town of Kajaani.","它建在一座旧造纸厂内，由附近的一条河流供能，而它排出的余热为周围卡亚尼镇的居民供暖。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","The shallows provide homes for hundreds of species while storing floodwaters, filtering pollutants from water, and protecting nearby communities from potentially destructive storm surges.","浅水区既为数百种物种提供栖息地，又能蓄积洪水、过滤水中污染物，保护附近社区免受可能造成破坏的风暴潮侵袭。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Pennsylvania farmers, to use one telling example, aren’t thinking about next year’s blue crab harvest in Maryland when they decide whether to spread animal waste on their fields, yet the runoff into nearby creeks can have enormous impact downstream.","举一个很能说明问题的例子：宾夕法尼亚州的农民决定是否把牲畜粪便撒在田里时，不会想着马里兰州明年的蓝蟹收成；然而，流入附近溪流的地表径流可能对下游造成巨大影响。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4 · 第36题 · 选项D","The Chesapeake Bay is described in Paragraph 1 as a headache for nearby communities.","第一段将切萨皮克湾描述为一个令周边社区头疼的问题。","选项"],["2016 英一 · 完形","Newlyweds traditionally move in with the wife’s parents and may live with them up to a year, until they can build a new house nearby.","按照传统，新婚夫妇搬去和女方父母同住，可能会住上长达一年，直到他们能在附近盖一所新房。",""]],"nearby.mp3",null],"nearly":[["ˈnɪə.li","ˈnɪər·li"],["中考","高中","TOEFL"],[["形容词","near",1],["名词","nearness",1]],[41,4.0,25,36,0],[["adv.","几乎；差不多；将近",41]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","An annual survey by the Chartered Institute of Public Finance and Accountancy puts it at nearly 800 across the UK; official statistics held by the Arts Council record 230 in England.","英国公共财政与会计特许协会的年度调查估计，全英国关闭的图书馆接近 800 家；而英格兰艺术委员会掌握的官方统计数据记载，英格兰关闭了 230 家。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","This concept has served as a central goal for curriculum developers, local school boards, business and community leaders, and policymakers ever since its introduction nearly 80 years ago.","自近80年前提出以来，这一理念一直是课程开发者、地方教育委员会、商界及社区领袖和政策制定者的核心目标。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","What began as a small neighborhood gathering blossomed into a massive cultural event, welcoming tens of thousands of people each year over nearly two decades before abruptly shutting down.","它起初只是一次小规模的街区聚会，后来发展成大型文化活动，近二十年来每年吸引数万人参加，最终却突然停办。","正文"],["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Nearly 75 years on, with the UK facing very different health challenges, it is clear that the model is out of date.","近 75 年过去，英国面临的健康挑战已大不相同，这种模式显然已经过时。","正文"],["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Customers in the past nearly always paid tips after receiving a service, such as at the conclusion of a restaurant meal, after getting a haircut or once a pizza was delivered.","过去，顾客几乎总是在享受服务后才付小费，例如吃完餐馆的一顿饭、理完发或收到披萨之后。","正文"],["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","A Reddit webpage devoted to the phenomenon, boasting nearly 50,000 members, showcases images of local desire paths adorned with signs instructing pedestrians to adhere to designated walkways, underscoring the rebellious nature inherent in these human-made tracks.","Reddit 上一个专门讨论这一现象的页面拥有近五万名成员，展示了各地愿望路径的照片；照片中的标牌要求行人只走指定步道，凸显出这些人踩出来的小路所固有的反叛意味。","正文"]],"nearly.mp3",{"r":[["后缀","-ly 表副词，通常缀于形容词后。"]],"d":[]}],"neat":[["niːt","nit"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["复数","neat"],["复数","neats"],["比较级","neater"],["最高级","neatest"],["副词","neatly",1],["名词","neatness",1],["形容词","unneat",1]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["adj.","整洁的；整齐的；有序的",1],["adj.","有条理的；爱整洁的",0],["adj.","小巧优雅的",0],["adj.","简洁的；睿智的；灵巧的",0],["adj.","好的；极好的",0],["adj.","未掺水的；纯的",0]],[["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Often appearing as trodden dirt tracks through otherwise neat green spaces, these routes of collective disobedience cut corners, bisect lawns and cross hills, representing the natural capability of people (and animals) to go from point A to point B most effectively.","这些集体“违规”开辟的路线通常是在原本整齐的绿地上踩出的小土路：它们抄近道、斜穿草坪、越过山丘，体现出人（和动物）以最高效率从甲地到乙地的天性。","正文"]],"neat.mp3",null],"necklace":[["ˈnek.ləs","ˈnek·lɪs"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研"],[["复数","necklaces"]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","项链",0],["v.","给（某人）戴火项链（将燃烧的轮胎挂在脖子上将其烧死）",0]],[],"necklace.mp3",{"r":[["词根","lac-,lic- 原意表示“诱惑；诱捕猎物的网”。多引申为美味、精细、甜美、柔和、喜爱。"]],"d":[]}],"needle":[["ˈniː.dᵊl","ˈni·dᵊl"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","GRE"],[["复数","needles"],["原形","needle"],["第三人称单数","needles"],["现在分词","needling"],["过去式","needled"],["过去分词","needled"],["形容词","needlelike",1],["名词","needler",1]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["n.","针；缝衣针",1],["n.","编织针",0],["n.","注射针；针头",0],["n.","指针",0],["n.","针叶；松针",0],["n.","唱针；磁针",0],["v.","刺激；故意招惹；（尤指）不断地数落",0]],[["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","The result is an embarrassment of historical riches, which brings its own needle-and-haystack problems.","由此产生了丰富得令人应接不暇的历史资料，也带来了大海捞针般的检索难题。","正文"]],"needle.mp3",null],"neighbourhood":[["ˈneɪ.bə.hʊd","ˈneɪ.bɚ.hʊd"],["高中","CET4","CET6"],[["复数","neighborhoods"]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","街区；城区；（统称）某街区（或城区）的居民",0],["n.","所在地；邻近的地方",0]],[],"neighbourhood.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neigh- = near, 表示“附近”。"],["后缀","-our 构成抽象名词或集体名词，如 ardour【热情】。"],["后缀","-hood 表名词，“时期，性质等”。"]],"d":[]}],"nest":[["nest","nest"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研"],[["复数","nests"],["原形","nest"],["第三人称单数","nests"],["现在分词","nesting"],["过去式","nested"],["过去分词","nested"]],[2,1.0,2,2,0],[["n.","鸟巢；鸟窝",1],["n.","巢穴；窝",0],["n.","藏匿处；秘密窝点",0],["n.","家；安乐窝",0],["n.","（套叠在一起的）一套物件",0],["v.","筑巢；巢居",0],["v.","嵌套（信息）",0],["n.","备用的钱;储备金",1]],[["2022 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Because of longer life spans, Americans are also boosting their savings to preserve their nest eggs, the TD Ameritrade study showed, which surveyed 2,000 adults between 40 to 79.","德美利证券对2000名40至79岁成年人进行的调查显示，由于寿命延长，美国人也在增加储蓄，以保住养老积蓄。","正文"],["2012 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","Beavers build dams and birds make nests.","河狸筑坝，鸟儿筑巢。","正文"]],"nest.mp3",{"r":[["词根","sid-,sed-,sess- = sit, 表示“坐”，来自拉丁语。"],["词根","neth- = below, 表示“下面”"]],"d":[["nestle","偎依；舒适地坐定；半隐半现地处于"],["nested","1. adj. 嵌套的，内装的 2. v. 筑巢；嵌入（nest的过去分词）"],["nesteia","n. 饥饿,禁食"],["nestful","n. 满巢,满窝"],["nesting","1. n. 嵌套；造巢；镶嵌 2. v. 为…筑巢；整天呆在家里；使套入（nest的ing形式）"]]}],"net":[["net","net"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL"],[["复数","nets"],["原形","net"],["第三人称单数","nets"],["现在分词","netting"],["过去式","netted"],["过去分词","netted"],["形容词","netless",1],["形容词","netlike",1],["形容词","netty",1],["名词","netter",1]],[25,3.5,9,17,3],[["n.","网；网状物",2],["n.","球门网",0],["n.","球网",0],["n.","有专门用途的网",0],["n.","（在计算机，尤指互联网上）搜寻信息，浏览信息",9],["adv.","净得的；纯的",0],["adj.","净得的；纯的",2],["adj.","净的",0],["adj.","最后的；最终的",8],["v.","净赚；净得",0],["v.","（尤指）用网捕捉（鱼等）",0],["v.","（巧妙地）捕获，得到",0],["v.","（将球）踢入球门，射入球门",0],["v.","用网覆盖",0],["n.","（为面临重大困难且无助的人提供帮助的）安全网，保障体制",3],["transitive verb","用网络覆盖，或像网络一样覆盖",1]],[["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","If the world is to meet its net-zero ambitions, we must think hard about how we can deliver sustainable computing and deliver more LUMIs.","如果世界要实现净零排放目标，我们就必须认真思考如何实现可持续计算，并建设更多像LUMI这样的超级计算机。","正文"],["2024 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Currently only 20 percent of the UK’s wood requirement is home-grown while it remains the second-largest net importer of timber in the world.","目前，英国所需木材只有20%产自本国，但它仍是全球第二大木材净进口国。","正文"],["2024 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Goodall added: “While food production and biodiversity health are clearly of critical importance, we need our land to also provide secure supplies of wood for construction, manufacturing and contribute to net-zero.”","古道尔补充说：“粮食生产和生物多样性的健康状况显然极其重要，但我们还需要土地为建筑业和制造业提供可靠的木材供应，并助力实现净零排放。”","正文"],["2024 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","While productive tree planting can deliver real financial benefits to rural economies and contribute to the UK’s net-zero strategy, the focus of government support continues to be on food production and the rewilding and planting of native woodland solely for biodiversity.","尽管为生产木材而植树能给农村经济带来实实在在的经济利益，并有助于英国的净零排放战略，但政府的支持仍集中在粮食生产，以及仅以生物多样性为目的的生态恢复和本土林地种植上。","正文"],["2023 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","The rules, which came into effect on Wednesday in England, are part of government plans to reduce the UK’s carbon emissions to net zero by 2050.","这些规定于周三在英格兰生效，是政府计划到2050年将英国碳排放降至净零的一部分。","正文"],["2021 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","That means more battles like the one now going on between the Justice Department and California, which enacted a tough net neutrality law in the wake of the FCC’s abdication.","这意味着，类似司法部与加利福尼亚州之间正在进行的争斗还会增多；加州在 FCC 弃守监管职责后制定了严格的网络中立性法律。","正文"]],"net.mp3",null],"network":[["ˈnet.wɜːk","ˈnetˌwɜrk"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[["复数","networks"],["原形","network"],["第三人称单数","networks"],["现在分词","networking"],["过去式","networked"],["过去分词","networked"],["名词","networker",1]],[36,4.0,14,22,4],[["n.","网络；网状系统",17],["n.","关系网；人际网；相互关系（或配合）的系统",10],["n.","（互联）网络",2],["n.","广播网；电视网",2],["v.","将…连接成网络",4],["v.","联播",0],["v.","建立工作关系",1]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","The network also connects Naples, Bologna, Florence and Turin.","这一铁路网络还连接那不勒斯、博洛尼亚、佛罗伦萨和都灵。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","With multiple networks and countless podcasts, a smartphone user selects what to hear and when.","有了众多广播网络和数不清的播客，智能手机用户可以自行选择听什么、何时听。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","If there’s congestion or, for example, a local train breaks down, the entire high-speed network is affected.","一旦发生线路拥堵，或例如某列普通列车抛锚，整个高铁网络都会受到影响。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Their North American tree-ring fire-scar network (NAFSN) provided the basis for a study published last month.","他们建立的北美树木年轮火灾疤痕网络（NAFSN）成为上月发表的一项研究的基础。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","RFI, the network operator, is the single largest European recovery fund beneficiary with planned investments of €24bn by 2026.","铁路网运营商 RFI 是欧洲复苏基金最大的单一受益者，计划在 2026 年前投资 240 亿欧元。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Since the 2008 launch of the high-speed rail network between Rome and Milan, trains have become the preferred means of travel across Italy for locals and tourists alike.","自 2008 年罗马至米兰高速铁路开通以来，火车已经成为本地人和游客在意大利出行的首选交通方式。","正文"]],"network.mp3",{"r":[],"d":[["networking","n. 联网"],["subnetwork","粒界网状组织"],["internetwork","网络"]]}],"neutral":[["ˈnjuː.trəl","ˈnu·trəl"],["CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL"],[["复数","neutrals"],["副词","neutrally",1],["名词","neutralness",1],["形容词","unneutral",1]],[3,1.5,2,2,1],[["adj.","中立的；持平的；无倾向性的",3],["adj.","中立国的；中立的",0],["adj.","中性的；不含褒贬义的",0],["adj.","不受影响的；没有倾向的",0],["adj.","素净的；淡素的；不鲜艳的",0],["adj.","中性的；非酸性又非碱性的",0],["adj.","中性的；不带电的",0],["n.","（汽车排挡）空挡",0],["n.","中立者；中立国",0],["n.","中性色；无彩色；素净色",0]],[["2021 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","You might feel your heart racing or your face turning red, but do whatever you can to remain neutral in both your words and actions.","你可能觉得心跳加速、脸颊发红，但无论如何都要尽量保持言语和举止平和。","正文"],["2012 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","What’s more, both boys and girls wore what were thought of as gender-neutral dresses.","而且，无论男孩还是女孩，都穿着当时被视为不分性别的连衣裙。","正文"],["2012 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2 · 第27题 · 选项D","According to Paragraph 2, which of the following is true of colours? Pink used to be a neutral colour in symbolizing genders.","根据第二段，以下关于颜色的哪项说法是正确的？粉红色过去在象征性别时不偏向任何一方。","选项"]],"neutral.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neutr- = middle, 表示“中间”。其中 ne- 表示否定 + utr- 相当于 either, 即不在任何一边, 也就是位于中间状态。"],["后缀","-al,-ial 表形容词，“…的”，一般缀于名词后。"]],"d":[["neutrally","中立"],["unneutral","非中立"],["neutralise","抵消"],["neutralism","中立"],["neutralist","中立"]]}],"new":[["njuː","nu"],["中考","高中"],[["比较级","newer"],["最高级","newest"],["形容词","newish",1],["名词","newness",1]],[318,5.0,43,210,45],[["adj.","刚出现的；新的；新近推出的",158],["adj.","新东西；新事物",1],["adj.","新买的",3],["adj.","没被用过的；未曾被人占有过的；崭新的",8],["adj.","有别于从前的；新颖的",56],["adj.","刚体验到的；初见的；不熟悉的",31],["adj.","初来乍到的；初学乍练的；新鲜的",15],["adj.","刚开始的；初始的；重新开始的",12],["adj.","（用于构成复合词）新的，新近的",4],["adj.","现代的；最新型的",8],["adj.","富有朝气的；生气勃勃的",0],["adj.","新近产生的；新开发的；时鲜的",5],["adj.","新出现的;新兴的",16],["adj.","新的；有别于从前的",1]],[["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","People report that broadcast music made workmen whistle new tunes.","人们说，广播里的音乐让工人们吹口哨吹出新曲子。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Between two great wars this technological innovation built a new kind of national consciousness.","在两次大战之间，这项技术创新塑造了一种新的国民共同意识。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","Battles increasingly depended on new military technologies such as radar and the proximity fuze.","战斗越来越依赖雷达、近炸引信等新型军事技术。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","These agencies and other government bodies should dramatically improve incentives to keep our current shows and attract new productions to Los Angeles.","这些机构和其他政府部门应大幅提高优惠力度，以留住现有剧组，并吸引新的制作项目来到洛杉矶。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","The development in 1915 of the popular new subject “general science” was another effort to train students to apply the principles of science to everyday, nonscience problems.","1915年，广受欢迎的新学科“普通科学”的出现，是另一项训练学生将科学原理应用于日常非科学问题的尝试。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Back then platforms such as Netflix, Amazon and Apple TV hemorrhaged billions of dollars to generate content to attract new subscribers, resulting in 633 scripted series being released that year.","那时，网飞、亚马逊和Apple TV等平台为了制作内容、吸引新订户，烧掉了数十亿美元，结果那一年播出了633部有剧本的剧集。","正文"]],"new.mp3",null],"nickname":[["ˈnɪk.neɪm","ˈnɪkˌneɪm；ˈnɪk·neɪm"],["CET6","考研","TOEFL"],[["复数","nicknames"],["原形","nickname"],["第三人称单数","nicknames"],["现在分词","nicknaming"],["过去式","nicknamed"],["过去分词","nicknamed"],["名词","nicknamer",1],["形容词","nicknameless",1]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["n.","绰号；诨名；外号",1],["v.","给…起绰号",0]],[["2013 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","They even had an affectionate nickname, “uccelli di passaggio,” birds of passage.","他们甚至有一个亲切的绰号：“uccelli di passaggio”，即“候鸟”。","正文"]],"nickname.mp3",{"r":[["词根","aug-,aux-,auth- = to increase 增长"],["词根","nom-,nomin-,nam- = name, 表示“名称，名字”。"]],"d":[]}],"nightmare":[["ˈnaɪt.meəʳ","ˈnɑɪtˌmeər"],["CET6","考研","IELTS","GRE"],[["复数","nightmares"],["形容词","nightmarish",1],["副词","nightmarishly",1]],[3,1.5,3,3,0],[["n.","噩梦；梦魇",1],["n.","可怕的经历；难以处理之事；噩梦",2]],[["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Without constant migration of digital assets, a nightmare about the foreseeable future is what keeps historians up at night: a historical record that abruptly stops when digital replace analog.","如果不持续迁移数字资产，历史学家便会被一个可预见的未来噩梦弄得夜不能寐：数字媒介取代模拟媒介之后，历史记录突然中断。","正文"],["2014 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Many of them instead become the kind of nuisance-lawsuit filer that makes the tort system a costly nightmare.","相反，其中许多人专门提起滋扰性诉讼，使侵权责任制度成为代价高昂的噩梦。","正文"],["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Those suffering from persistent nightmares should seek help from a therapist.","长期受噩梦困扰的人应向治疗师求助。","正文"]],"nightmare.mp3",{"r":[["词根","noct-,nyct-,night = night, 表示“夜晚”。 noct- 源自拉丁语，nyct- 源自希腊语，night 源自古英语（日耳曼语），他们都来源于原始印欧语 *nekwt- (night)。"]],"d":[["nightmarish","adj. 恶梦似的,不愉快的"]]}],"nominal":[["ˈnɒm.ɪ.nᵊl","ˈnɑm·ə·nᵊl"],["CET6","考研","IELTS","GRE"],[["复数","nominals"],["副词","nominally",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["adj.","名义上的；有名无实的",0],["adj.","很小的；象征性的",0],["adj.","名词性的；名词的",0]],[],"nominal.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nom-,nomin-,nam- = name, 表示“名称，名字”。"],["后缀","-al,-ial 表形容词，“…的”，一般缀于名词后。"]],"d":[["pronominal","adj. 代词的,代词性质的"],["binominal","adj. 二名制的,种名前加属名的"],["nominally","名义上"],["cognominal","adj. 同名的,同姓的"],["nominalize","v. 使转变为名词,使名词化"]]}],"nominate":[["ˈnɒm.ɪ.neɪt","ˈnɑm·əˌneɪt"],["CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS","GRE"],[["原形","nominate"],["第三人称单数","nominates"],["现在分词","nominating"],["过去式","nominated"],["过去分词","nominated"],["形容词","nominatable",1],["名词","nominator",1],["名词","nominee",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["v.","提名；推荐",0],["v.","任命；指派",0],["v.","挑选，指定（时间、日期、名称等）",0]],[],"nominate.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nom-,nomin-,nam- = name, 表示“名称，名字”。"],["后缀","-ate 表动词，“做，造成”。"]],"d":[["nominative","主格"],["nominator","提名"],["nomination","提名"]]}],"naked":[["ˈneɪ.kɪd","ˈneɪ·kɪd"],["CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["副词","nakedly",1],["名词","nakedness",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["adj.","裸体的；裸露的；不穿衣服的",0],["adj.","无遮盖的；裸露的",0],["adj.","直白的；露骨的；毫不掩饰的",0],["adj.","缺乏保护；无力自卫",0]],[],"naked.mp3",{"r":[["后缀","-ed 形容词后缀，加在名词后表示“如...的”；加在动词后表示“被...的”。"]],"d":[["nakedness","n. 裸出"],["stark-naked","一丝不挂"],["mother-naked","adj. 像初出娘胎时一丝不挂的"]]}],"nail":[["neɪl","neɪl"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL"],[["复数","nails"],["原形","nail"],["第三人称单数","nails"],["现在分词","nailing"],["过去式","nailed"],["过去分词","nailed"],["名词","nailer",1]],[23,3.5,2,17,1],[["n.","指甲；趾甲",3],["n.","钉；钉子",20],["v.","（用钉子）钉牢，固定",0],["v.","抓获并证明有罪；抓住",0],["v.","证明…不属实；揭露；揭发",0],["v.","（尤指体育运动中）获得，赢得，击中",0]],[["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Why had the Romans buried a million nails?","罗马人为什么要埋下一百万枚钉子？","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","The nail hoard was discovered in 1960 in a four-metre-deep pit covered by two metres of gravel.","这批钉子于1960年在一个四米深、上面覆盖着两米厚砾石的坑中被发现。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","The Romans buried the nails so deep that they would not be discovered for almost two millennia.","罗马人把钉子埋得如此深，以至于将近两千年后才有人发现。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","This was an attempt to recover the valuable nails, which could be reused after sifting the ashes.","他们这样做是为了找回贵重的钉子：只要筛过灰烬，这些钉子就能再次使用。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Nails themselves have changed over the years, but Sichel studied them because they haven’t changed much.","这些年钉子本身也有所变化，但西切尔之所以研究钉子，恰恰是因为它们变化不大。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Later civilisations would value the skilled blacksmith’s labour in a nail even more than the raw material.","后来的文明甚至会认为，钉子里凝结的熟练铁匠的劳动，比原材料更有价值。","正文"]],"nail.mp3",{"r":[["词根","onych-,onycho-,onyx- = nail, 表示“甲, 爪”，源自希腊语 onyx = nail。和源自拉丁语的 ungu-，源自古英语（日耳曼语）的 nail 同源。"]],"d":[["hobnail","n. 乡下佬；鞋钉，平头钉"],["nailer","n. 制钉者；自动敲钉机；敲钉者；[俚]能手"],["nailery","n. 制钉工厂"],["nailing","adj. [俚]极好的；出色的；敲钉用的"],["toenail","n. 脚趾甲；斜钉"]]}],"naive":[["naɪˈiːv","nɑˈiv"],["CET6","考研","GRE"],[["比较级","naiver"],["最高级","naivest"],["副词","naively",1],["名词","naiveness",1]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["adj.","缺乏经验的；幼稚的；无知的；轻信的",1],["adj.","天真的；率直的",0],["adj.","稚拙派的（简单质朴，色彩明快）",0]],[["2007 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","They should exhibit strong interest and respect for whatever currently interests their fledgling adult (as naive or ill conceived as it may seem) while becoming a partner in exploring options for the future.","他们应对刚成年的子女目前感兴趣的一切表现出浓厚兴趣和尊重（无论这些兴趣看起来多么天真或欠考虑），同时成为他们探索未来选择的伙伴。","正文"]],"naive.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nat-,nai- = born, 表示“出生的”，来自古典拉丁语 gnasci，由词根 gen-（出生，产生）组成。"]],"d":[]}],"namely":[["ˈneɪm.li","ˈneɪm·li"],["CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["adv.","即；也就是",0]],[],"namely.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nom-,nomin-,nam- = name, 表示“名称，名字”。"],["后缀","-ly 表副词，通常缀于形容词后。"]],"d":[]}],"nap":[["næp","næp"],["CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[["复数","naps"],["原形","nap"],["第三人称单数","naps"],["现在分词","napping"],["过去式","napped"],["过去分词","napped"],["形容词","napless",1],["形容词","napped",1],["名词","napper",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","（日间的）小睡，打盹",0],["n.","（某些织物表面的）短绒毛",0],["n.","赛马情报；赛马结果预测",0],["v.","打盹，小睡（尤指日间）",0]],[],"nap.mp3",null],"naughty":[["ˈnɔː.ti","ˈnɔ·t̬i；ˈnɑt̬·i"],["CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL"],[["比较级","naughtier"],["最高级","naughtiest"],["副词","naughtily",1],["名词","naughtiness",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["adj.","顽皮的；淘气的；不听话的",0],["adj.","粗俗的；下流的",0]],[],"naughty.mp3",{"r":[["后缀","-y 表形容词，加在名词后变成形容词。"]],"d":[]}],"none":[["nʌn","nʌn"],["中考","高中"],[],[11,2.5,9,8,0],[["pron.","没有一个；毫无",11],["adv.","（与 the 加比较级连用）一点都不，绝无",0],["adv.","（与 too 加形容词或副词连用）绝不，不怎么",0]],[["2019 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","None of this is about writing off the individual.","这并不是要否定个人的作用。","正文"],["2016 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","At the next election none of the big parties seem likely to endorse this sentiment.","在下一次选举中，各主要政党似乎都不大可能支持这种理念。","正文"],["2012 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","At the same time, the policy addresses none of the truly thorny questions about homework.","与此同时，这项政策丝毫没有触及有关家庭作业的真正棘手问题。","正文"],["2011 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","These designers came to exert enormous influence on the course of American architecture, but none more so than Mies.","这些设计师后来对美国建筑的发展产生了巨大影响，而密斯的影响无人能及。","正文"],["2007 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Anders Ericsson, a 58-year-old psychology professor at Florida State University, says he believes strongly in “none of the above.”","佛罗里达州立大学58岁的心理学教授安德斯·埃里克森说，他坚信答案是“以上皆非”。","正文"],["2007 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Here are a few guesses: a) certain astrological signs confer superior soccer skills; b) winter-born babies tend to have higher oxygen capacity, which increases soccer stamina; c) soccer-mad parents are more likely to conceive children in springtime, at the annual peak of soccer mania; d) none of the above.","这里有几种猜测：a）某些星座赋予人更出色的足球技能；b）冬季出生的婴儿往往有更高的摄氧能力，从而增强足球比赛中的耐力；c）痴迷足球的父母更可能在春季，也就是每年足球热最盛的时候受孕；d）以上皆非。","正文"]],"none.mp3",{"r":[["前缀","non- 表示“不，非”。"]],"d":[["nonetheless","adv. 虽然如此,但是"]]}],"nonsense":[["ˈnɒn.sᵊns","ˈnɑnˌsens"],["CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL"],[["复数","nonsenses"],["形容词","nonsensical",1],["副词","nonsensically",1],["名词","nonsensicalness",1]],[5,2.0,3,3,2],[["n.","谬论；胡扯；胡言乱语",5],["n.","毫无意义的话；没有意义的文章",0],["n.","愚蠢的行为；冒失；不可接受的行为",0]],[["2019 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","(46) There is a great deal of this kind of nonsense in the medical journals which, when taken up by broadcasters and the lay press, generates both health scares and short-lived dietary enthusiasms.","（46）医学期刊里有大量此类荒谬内容；广播媒体和面向大众的报刊一旦加以报道，便会同时引发健康恐慌和昙花一现的饮食热潮。","正文"],["2015 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","As a linguist once said, “You can get people to think it’s nonsense at the same time that you buy into it.”","正如一位语言学家曾说：“你可以让人们觉得它是一派胡言，而自己同时又信了这一套。”","正文"],["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Lots of Americans bought that nonsense, and over three decades, some 10 million smokers went to early graves.","许多美国人相信了这些荒谬说法，而在三十年间，约有一千万吸烟者过早去世。","正文"],["2015 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3 · 第35题 · 选项B","Which of the following statements is true about office speak? Linguists believe it to be nonsense.","下列关于办公室用语的哪项说法是正确的？语言学家认为这种用语毫无意义。","选项"],["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2 · 第26题 · 选项D","An argument made by supporters of smoking was that antismoking people were usually talking nonsense.","吸烟支持者曾提出的一个论点是，反对吸烟的人通常都在胡说八道。","选项"]],"nonsense.mp3",{"r":[["前缀","non- 表示“不，非”。"],["词根","sens-,sent- = feel, 表示“感觉”，来自拉丁语。"]],"d":[["nononsense","adj. 不开玩笑的,正经的"],["no-nonsense","adj. 实际的,严肃的"],["nonsensical","adj. 无意义的;荒谬的;愚蠢的"]]}],"nuclear":[["ˈnjuː.klɪəʳ","ˈnu·kli·ər"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL"],[],[12,2.5,3,10,1],[["adj.","原子能的；核能的",11],["adj.","核武器的",0],["adj.","核子的；原子核的",0],["n.","（由父母与子女组成的）核心家庭",1]],[["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","In a paper published in the Journal of Child Psychology and Psychiatry, researchers said that the western nuclear family was a recent invention which broke with evolutionary history.","研究人员在发表于《儿童心理学与精神病学杂志》的一篇论文中表示，西方核心家庭是近代才出现的形式，背离了人类的进化历史。","正文"],["2012 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Permission to run a nuclear plant is a public trust.","核电站的运营许可是一项公众托付。","正文"],["2012 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Entergy runs 11 other reactors in the United States, including Pilgrim Nuclear station in Plymouth.","安特吉在美国还运营着另外11座反应堆，其中包括普利茅斯的朝圣者核电站。","正文"],["2012 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","The conflict has been surfacing since 2002, when the corporation bought Vermont’s only nuclear power plant, an aging reactor in Vernon.","这场冲突从2002年开始浮现：当时该公司收购了佛蒙特州唯一的核电站，即弗农的一座老旧反应堆。","正文"],["2012 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","But as the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) reviews the company’s application, it should keep in mind what promises from Entergy are worth.","但在核管理委员会（NRC）审查该公司的申请时，应当牢记安特吉的承诺究竟有多大分量。","正文"],["2012 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Now the company is suddenly claiming that the 2002 agreement is invalid because of the 2006 legislation, and that only the federal government has regulatory power over nuclear issues.","如今该公司突然声称，由于2006年的立法，2002年的协议无效，而且只有联邦政府才有权监管核能事务。","正文"]],"nuclear.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nucle-,nucl-,nucleo- = kernel, 表示“核”。来源于拉丁语。"]],"d":[["thermonuclear","adj. 高热原子核反应的"],["mononuclear","单核"],["anuclear","adj. 无核的；无细胞核的"],["binuclear","n. 传记"],["nonnuclear","非核"]]}],"nucleus":[["ˈnjuː.kli.əs","ˈnu·kli·əs"],["CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS","GRE"],[["复数","nuclei"],["复数","nucleuses"]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","核；原子核",0],["n.","细胞核",0],["n.","核心；中心",0]],[],"nucleus.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nucle-,nucl-,nucleo- = kernel, 表示“核”。来源于拉丁语。"]],"d":[["nucleuses","n. 核，核心；原子核"],["pronucleus","前核"],["subnucleus","亚核"],["meganucleus","巨核"],["paranucleus","n. 副核"]]}],"nourish":[["ˈnʌr.ɪʃ","ˈnɜr·ɪʃ；ˈnʌr·ɪʃ"],["CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS","GRE"],[["原形","nourish"],["第三人称单数","nourishes"],["现在分词","nourishing"],["过去式","nourished"],["过去分词","nourished"],["名词","nourisher",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["v.","抚养；滋养；养育",0],["v.","培养，促进（情绪、观点等）",0]],[],"nourish.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nour-,nurs- 表示“喂养，营养”。"],["后缀","-ish 表动词，“造成…”。"]],"d":[["nourishment","n. 食物, 滋养品"],["malnourished","营养不良"],["nourishing","adj. 有营养的,滋养多的"],["undernourish","vt. 使营养不足,使吃不饱"],["ill-nourished","营养不良"]]}],"novel":[["ˈnɒv.ᵊl","ˈnɑv·əl"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["复数","novels"],["形容词","novelistic",1],["副词","novelistically",1],["形容词","novelish",1],["副词","novelly",1]],[15,3.0,9,5,1],[["n.","（长篇）小说",9],["adj.","新颖的；与众不同的；珍奇的",6]],[["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","New, disruptive technology sometimes demands novel applications of the Constitution’s protections.","具有颠覆性的新技术有时需要宪法保护条款以新的方式适用。","正文"],["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","He agreed to join because he “found the foresight behind the establishment of the SBoRE to be novel, unique and likely to have a lasting impact.","他同意加入，是因为他“认为设立SBoRE的远见新颖、独特，而且很可能产生持久影响。","正文"],["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Orin Kerr, a law professor, compares the explosion and accessibility of digital information in the 21st century with the establishment of automobile use as a virtual necessity of life in the 20th: The justices had to specify novel rules for the new personal domain of the passenger car then; they must sort out how the Fourth Amendment applies to digital information now.","法学教授奥林·克尔将21世纪数字信息的激增与获取便捷，比作20世纪汽车逐渐成为生活中几乎不可缺少的东西：当年，大法官们不得不针对作为新私人空间的乘用汽车制定新规则；如今，他们必须厘清第四修正案如何适用于数字信息。","正文"],["2012 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Sometimes years are required for truly novel discovery claims to be accepted and appreciated.","有时，一项真正新颖的发现主张需要多年才能获得认可和赏识。","正文"],["2001 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 5","Curiously, some two-and-a-half years and two novels later, my experiment in what the Americans term “downshifting” has turned my tired excuse into an absolute reality.","有趣的是，大约两年半和两部小说之后，我尝试的这种美国人称为“放慢生活节奏”的生活方式，已使我当初那句老掉牙的借口变成了实实在在的现实。","正文"],["2025 英二 · 写作 · Part A · 第47题","Suppose you are planning a short play based on a classic Chinese novel.","假设你正筹划一部改编自中国古典小说的短剧。",""]],"novel.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nov- = new, 表示“新的”。"],["后缀","-el 表名词，“人或物”。"]],"d":[["novelty","n. 新奇；新奇的事物；新颖小巧而廉价的物品"],["novella","n. 短篇故事；中篇小说"],["novelist","n. 小说家"],["novelize","vt. 使小说化；编成小说"],["antinovel","n. 非正统派小说;非传统小说"]]}],"novelty":[["ˈnɒv.ᵊl.ti","ˈnɑv·əl·ti"],["CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS","GRE"],[["复数","novelties"]],[3,1.5,2,1,1],[["n.","新奇；新颖；新鲜",2],["n.","新奇的事物（或人、环境）",0],["n.","廉价小饰物；小玩意儿",0],["adj.","新奇的；风格独特的",1]],[["2012 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Second, novelty itself frequently provokes disbelief.","其次，新颖本身往往会引发怀疑。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 完形","They started out as a novelty feature, but as their use has grown, their benefits have extended within our technologically advanced world.","起初，它们只是一项新奇的功能，但随着应用日益广泛，在当今技术先进的世界里，它们带来的益处也不断扩大。",""],["2012 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3 · 第35题 · 选项A","Which of the following would be the best title of the text? Novelty as an Engine of Scientific Development.","以下哪项最适合作为本文的标题？新颖性：科学发展的动力。","选项"]],"novelty.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nov- = new, 表示“新的”。"],["后缀","-el 表名词，“人或物”。"],["后缀","-ty 表名词，用在形容词后，把形容词变成名词。"]],"d":[]}],"nowadays":[["ˈnaʊ.ə.deɪz","ˈnɑʊ·əˌdeɪz"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL"],[],[8,2.5,6,5,0],[["adv.","现今；现在；目前",8]],[["2019 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","There has been a kind of inflationary process at work: (47) nowadays anyone applying for a research post has to have published twice the number of papers that would have been required for the same post only 10 years ago.","一种类似通货膨胀的过程一直在起作用：（47）如今，申请某个研究职位的人必须发表的论文数量，是仅仅十年前申请同一职位所需数量的两倍。","正文"],["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","I think that, for the majority of scientific papers nowadays, statistical review is more essential than expert review,” he says.","我认为，如今对大多数科学论文来说，统计学评审比专家评审更为重要。”他说。","正文"],["2000 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Nowadays the number of births, like the age of death, has become average.","如今，生育子女的数量，就像死亡年龄一样，趋于平均。","正文"],["2000 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","(35) Additional social stresses may also occur because of the population explosion or problems arising from mass migration movements — themselves made relatively easy nowadays by modern means of transport.","（35）人口激增，或大规模人口迁移引发的问题，也可能造成额外的社会压力；现代交通工具使这类迁移相对容易。","正文"],["2000 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","For example, (34) in the early industrialized countries of Europe the process of industrialization — with all the far-reaching changes in social patterns that followed — was spread over nearly a century, whereas nowadays a developing nation may undergo the same process in a decade or so.","例如，（34）在欧洲那些早期实现工业化的国家，工业化的过程及其随后带来的所有深远的社会形态变化，延续了近一个世纪；而如今，一个发展中国家可能在十年左右经历同样的过程。","正文"],["2018 英二 · 翻译","Nowadays, his reading material has changed from science fiction and reference books: recently, he revealed that he reads at least 50 nonfiction books a year.","如今，他读的书已不再以科幻小说和工具书为主：最近他透露，自己每年至少读 50 本非虚构类书籍。",""]],"nowadays.mp3",null],"nowhere":[["ˈnəʊ.weəʳ","ˈnoʊˌhweər"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[],[3,1.5,3,2,0],[["adv.","无处；哪里都不",3]],[["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","Nothing is absolutely safe, nowhere.","没有任何东西在任何地方是绝对安全的。","正文"],["2009 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","According to the standard history of American philosophy, nowhere else in colonial America was “so much importance attached to intellectual pursuits.”","按照美国哲学的标准历史叙述，在殖民地时期的美国，没有其他地方“如此重视知识活动”。","正文"],["2000 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2 · 第18题 · 选项D","Which of the following would be the best title for the passage? Human Evolution Going Nowhere.","下列哪一项最适合作为这篇文章的标题？《人类进化停滞不前》。","选项"]],"nowhere.mp3",null],"nostalgic":[["nɒsˈtæl.dʒɪk","nɑːˈstæl.dʒɪk"],[],[["复数","nostalgics"],["副词","nostalgically",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["adj.","怀旧；念旧",0]],[],"nostalgic.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nost- = home, 表示“家”。"],["词根","alg- = pain, 表示“痛”。"],["后缀","-ic 表形容词，“…的”。"]],"d":[]}],"notable":[["ˈnəʊ.tə.bᵊl","ˈnoʊ·t̬ə·bəl"],["CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS","GRE"],[["复数","notables"],["名词","notableness",1],["副词","notably",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["adj.","值得注意的；显著的；重要的",0],["n.","名人；重要人物",0]],[],"notable.mp3",{"r":[["词根","not- = know, 表示“知道，注意”，和表示知道的词根 gn- 同源。"],["后缀","-able 一般缀于动词后，构成形容词，表示“可…的，能…”。"]],"d":[["notably","adv. 显著地；尤其"],["notability","n. 显著;值得注意 显著的人;名人"]]}],"nothing":[["ˈnʌθ.ɪŋ","ˈnʌθ·ɪŋ"],["中考","高中","IELTS"],[["复数","nothings"],["名词","nothingness",1]],[26,3.5,19,21,1],[["pron.","没有什么；没有一件东西",25],["pron.","无关紧要的东西；毫无趣味的事",1]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","In return for all of this, you’ll be asked for precisely nothing.","享受这一切，你什么也无需付出。","正文"],["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","It is all too easy to feel paralysed in the face of daunting problems such as climate change and to do nothing.","面对气候变化等令人望而生畏的问题，人很容易感到无能为力，因而什么也不做。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","Nothing is absolutely safe, nowhere.","没有任何东西在任何地方是绝对安全的。","正文"],["2021 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Even Mark Twain, a man who enjoyed a hearty laugh, said that when it came to photographic portraits there could be “nothing more damning than a silly, foolish smile fixed forever”.","就连爱开怀大笑的马克·吐温也说，拍摄肖像照时，\"再没有什么比永远定格的愚蠢傻笑更丢人的了\"。","正文"],["2018 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Nothing is necessarily gained by forcing students to learn geometry at a graffitied desk stuck with generations of discarded chewing gum.","强迫学生坐在满是涂鸦、粘着几代人丢弃的口香糖的课桌前学几何，并不一定能让他们有所收获。","正文"],["2017 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Opposition to telescopes on Mauna Kea is nothing new.","反对在莫纳克亚山建造望远镜并非新鲜事。","正文"]],"nothing.mp3",null],"notice":[["ˈnəʊ.tɪs","ˈnoʊ·t̬ɪs"],["中考","高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["复数","notices"],["原形","notice"],["第三人称单数","notices"],["现在分词","noticing"],["过去式","noticed"],["过去分词","noticed"],["名词","noticer",1]],[26,3.5,20,8,0],[["v.","看（或听）到；注意到；意识到",10],["v.","注意；留意",2],["n.","通告；布告；通知",10],["n.","公告牌；警示牌",0],["n.","启事；声明",0],["n.","（会议、宗教活动等开头或结尾时的）通知",0],["n.","注意；理会；察觉",1],["n.","预告；警告",3],["n.","辞职信；搬迁通知",0],["n.","（报刊上对书籍、戏剧等的）评论，短评",0]],[["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","But inventions shape all of us and it is worth noticing when techno-social habits do change, and asking whether to control them a bit or shield the youngest.","但发明会塑造我们每一个人。技术与社会习惯确实发生变化时，值得留意，并思考是否要稍加约束，或保护最年幼的人。","正文"],["2023 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Teenagers are particularly sensitive to social rewards — winning the game, impressing a new friend, getting that boy to notice you.","青少年对社交回报尤其敏感——赢得比赛、给新朋友留下深刻印象，或让心仪的男孩注意到自己。","正文"],["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Long gone are the days when a boss could simply give an employee contractual notice.","老板只需按合同规定通知员工一声就能解雇人的日子，早已一去不复返。","正文"],["2016 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","Have you ever noticed how much children laugh?","你有没有注意到孩子们笑得有多频繁？","正文"],["2008 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","(49) He adds humbly that perhaps he was “superior to the common run of men in noticing things which easily escape attention, and in observing them carefully.”","（49）他又谦逊地补充说，也许自己“比一般人更善于注意那些容易被忽略的事物，并仔细观察它们”。","正文"],["2007 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","That may change fast: lots of proposed data-security legislation is now doing the rounds in Washington, D.C. Meanwhile, the theft of information about some 40 million credit-card accounts in America, disclosed on June 17th, overshadowed a hugely important decision a day earlier by America’s Federal Trade Commission (FTC) that puts corporate America on notice that regulators will act if firms fail to provide adequate data security.","这种情况可能很快改变：目前，华盛顿特区正有多项有关数据安全的立法提案在各方之间流转。与此同时，美国约4000万个信用卡账户的信息遭窃一事于6月17日披露，盖过了美国联邦贸易委员会（FTC）前一天作出的一项极其重要的决定的风头：监管机构已向全美企业发出警告，如果公司未能充分保障数据安全，监管者就会采取行动。","正文"]],"notice.mp3",{"r":[["词根","not- = know, 表示“知道，注意”，和表示知道的词根 gn- 同源。"]],"d":[["noticeable","显而易见的"],["unnoticed","adj. 未被觉察到的,未被注意到的"],["forenotice","n. 预告"],["noticeably","adv. 显著地,明显地"]]}],"notify":[["ˈnəʊ.tɪ.faɪ","ˈnoʊ·t̬ɪˌfɑɪ"],["CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[["原形","notify"],["第三人称单数","notifies"],["现在分词","notifying"],["过去式","notified"],["过去分词","notified"],["名词","notifier",1]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["v.","（正式）通报，通知",1]],[["2024 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","“The American Medical Association advises physicians that in situations where clear evidence of substantial driving impairment implies a strong threat to patient and public safety, and where the physician’s advice to discontinue driving privileges is ignored, it is desirable and ethical to notify the Department of Motor Vehicles,” Menke wrote.","门克写道：“美国医学会建议医生：如果有明确证据表明患者驾驶能力严重受损，意味着对患者本人和公众安全构成重大威胁，而患者又不听从医生关于放弃驾车权的劝告，那么通知机动车管理部门是适当且合乎职业伦理的。”","正文"]],"notify.mp3",{"r":[["词根","not- = know, 表示“知道，注意”，和表示知道的词根 gn- 同源。"],["后缀","-fy,-ify 缀于名词或形容词后，构成表示“使成…”“…化”“作成…”等意思的动词"]],"d":[["notification","通知"],["notifier","n. 通告人，通知人"],["notifiable","adj. 须申报的"]]}],"notorious":[["nəʊˈtɔː.ri.əs","nəˈtɔr·i·əs"],["CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS","GRE"],[["副词","notoriously",1]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["adj.","声名狼藉的；臭名昭著的",1]],[["2002 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","If you are part of the group which you are addressing, you will be in a position to know the experiences and problems which are common to all of you and it’ll be appropriate for you to make a passing remark about the inedible canteen food or the chairman’s notorious bad taste in ties.","如果你本就是听众群体的一员，就能了解大家共同的经历和问题；此时，顺带调侃食堂饭菜难以下咽，或主席那出了名的领带品味之差，就很合适。","正文"]],"notorious.mp3",{"r":[["词根","not- = know, 表示“知道，注意”，和表示知道的词根 gn- 同源。"],["后缀","-ous,-itious,-eous,-ious,-uous 表形容词，表示“…的”，用于化学领域表示“亚酸的，低价（金属）的”。"]],"d":[["notoriously","adv. 恶名昭彰地,声名狼藉地 著名地,众所周知地"]]}],"notwithstanding":[["ˌnɒt.wɪðˈstæn.dɪŋ","ˌnɑt·wɪθˈstæn·dɪŋ"],["CET6","考研","TOEFL"],[],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["prep.","虽然；尽管",0],["adv.","尽管如此",0],["conj.","尽管如此",0]],[],"notwithstanding.mp3",{"r":[["前缀","with- 表示“向后，相反”。"],["词根","st-,sta-,stat-,stan-,stant-,stin- = stand, 表示“站、立”。"],["后缀","-ing 表形容词，“正…的”，“令人…的”。"]],"d":[]}],"nuisance":[["ˈnjuː.sᵊns","ˈnu·səns"],["CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[["复数","nuisances"]],[2,1.0,2,1,0],[["n.","麻烦事；讨厌的人（或东西）",2],["n.","妨害行为",0]],[["2014 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Many of them instead become the kind of nuisance-lawsuit filer that makes the tort system a costly nightmare.","相反，其中许多人专门提起滋扰性诉讼，使侵权责任制度成为代价高昂的噩梦。","正文"],["2025 英二 · 完形","Yet another factor that you might be worried about is being a nuisance or inconveniencing the person you go to for help.","还有一个你可能担忧的因素：自己会不会成为累赘，或给求助对象带来不便。",""]],"nuisance.mp3",{"r":[["词根","noc-,nox- = hurt, poison, 表示“伤害，毒”。"],["后缀","-ance 表名词，“性质，状况”，一般缀于动词后。"]],"d":[]}],"numb":[["nʌm","nʌm"],["高中","考研","TOEFL","IELTS","GRE"],[["原形","numb"],["第三人称单数","numbs"],["现在分词","numbing"],["过去式","numbed"],["过去分词","numbed"],["副词","numbly",1],["名词","numbness",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["adj.","麻木的；失去知觉的",0],["adj.","麻木的；迟钝的；呆滞的",0],["v.","使失去知觉；使麻木",0],["v.","使麻木；使迟钝",0]],[],"numb.mp3",null],"numerical":[["njuːˈmer.ɪ.kᵊl","nuˈmer·ɪ·kəl"],["CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["副词","numerically",1]],[4,1.5,3,3,0],[["adj.","数字的；用数字表示的",4]],[["2019 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","The H-2A visa has no numerical cap, unlike the H-2B visa for nonagricultural work, which is limited to 66,000 a year.","H-2A签证没有数量上限，而用于非农业工作的H-2B签证每年限发6.6万份。","正文"],["2007 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","IQ tests ask you to complete verbal and visual analogies, to envision paper after it has been folded and cut, and to deduce numerical sequences, among other similar tasks.","智商测试要求受试者完成词语和图形类比、想象纸张折叠裁剪后的形状、推断数字序列等类似任务。","正文"],["2007 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","It’s not obvious how the capacity to visualize objects and to figure out numerical patterns suits one to answer questions that have eluded some of the best poets and philosophers.","想象物体和找出数字规律的能力，究竟如何使一个人适合回答连一些最杰出的诗人和哲学家都无法解答的问题，这并不显而易见。","正文"],["2014 英二 · 完形","While such numerical standards seem straightforward, they are not.","尽管这些数字标准看似简单明了，事实却并非如此。",""]],"numerical.mp3",{"r":[["词根","numer- = number, 表示“数目”。"],["后缀","-ic 表形容词，“…的”。"],["后缀","-al,-ial 表形容词，“…的”，一般缀于名词后。"]],"d":[["numerically","数字"]]}],"numerous":[["ˈnjuː.mə.rəs","ˈnu·mər·əs"],["CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS","GRE"],[["副词","numerously",1],["名词","numerousness",1]],[2,1.0,2,1,0],[["adj.","众多的；许多的",2]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","This is why the recent severe delays caused by numerous maintenance works have thrown the rail industry into chaos at a time when most people head on holiday, which matters for business in a country where tourism accounts for 10 percent of GDP.","正因如此，近期大量维修工程造成的严重晚点，才会在大多数人外出度假之际使铁路业陷入混乱；对于旅游业占国内生产总值 10% 的意大利，这也关系到经济利益。","正文"],["2013 英一 · 完形","This scale took numerous factors into consideration.","这一评分标准考虑了许多因素。",""]],"numerous.mp3",{"r":[["词根","numer- = number, 表示“数目”。"],["后缀","-ous,-itious,-eous,-ious,-uous 表形容词，表示“…的”，用于化学领域表示“亚酸的，低价（金属）的”。"]],"d":[]}],"nursery":[["ˈnɜː.sᵊr.i","ˈnɜr·sər·i"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[["复数","nurseries"]],[5,2.0,3,4,0],[["n.","（供游戏的）儿童室",0],["n.","婴儿室",1],["n.","苗圃",1],["adj.","幼儿教育的",0],["n.","幼儿园，托儿所",3]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","Christopher Kettle, Biodiversity International’s director for forest genetic resources and restoration in Rome, says that the need for infrastructure — things such as mechanisms for collecting and storing seeds, and nurseries to raise seedlings — might be most desperate here because many trees are ‘masting’ species, which don’t produce seeds every year.","国际生物多样性组织驻罗马的森林遗传资源与恢复事务主任克里斯托弗·凯特尔表示，这里可能最迫切需要基础设施，例如采集和储存种子的机制、培育树苗的苗圃，因为许多树木属于间歇性结籽的物种，并非每年都会产种。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","In Germany, one scheme has paired an old people’s home with a nursery.","在德国，有一个项目将养老院与幼儿园结成伙伴。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","An infant born to a hunter-gatherer society could have more than ten caregivers — this contrasts starkly to nursery settings in the UK where regulations call for a ratio of one carer to four children aged two to three.","狩猎采集社会出生的婴儿可能有十多名照护者；与之形成鲜明对比的是，英国托儿机构的规定是每四名两至三岁儿童配备一名照护者。","正文"],["2012 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","When nursery colours were introduced, pink was actually considered the more masculine colour, a pastel version of red, which was associated with strength.","最初推出婴儿房专用色时，粉红色实际上被认为是更具男性气质的颜色，因为它是红色的淡色调，而红色与力量联系在一起。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2 · 第29题","According to Paragraph 6, what can we learn about the nurseries in the UK?","根据第六段，关于英国的托儿机构我们可以了解到什么？","题干"]],"nursery.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nour-,nurs- 表示“喂养，营养”。"],["后缀","-ery 表名词，“场所，地点”。"]],"d":[["nurseryman","n. 花圃工人; 园丁; 苗木培育工"],["nurserymaid","保姆"]]}],"nurture":[["ˈnɜː.tʃəʳ","ˈnɜr·tʃər"],["CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS","GRE"],[["复数","nurtures"],["原形","nurture"],["第三人称单数","nurtures"],["现在分词","nurturing"],["过去式","nurtured"],["过去分词","nurtured"],["名词","nurturer",1],["形容词","nurtureless",1]],[2,1.0,2,1,0],[["v.","养育；养护；培养",1],["v.","扶持；帮助；支持",0],["v.","滋长；助长",0],["n.","养育；培养",1]],[["2012 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","In place of Thomas Carlyle, Britain nurtured Christopher Hill, EP Thompson and Eric Hobsbawm.","取代托马斯·卡莱尔的，是英国培养出的克里斯托弗·希尔、E. P. 汤普森和埃里克·霍布斯鲍姆。","正文"],["2007 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1 · 第24题 · 选项D","Ericsson and his colleagues believe that high achievers owe their success mostly to nurture.","埃里克森和他的同事认为，成就卓越者的成功主要归功于后天培养。","选项"]],"nurture.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nour-,nurs- 表示“喂养，营养”。"]],"d":[["nurturance","n. 养育,培养"]]}],"nut":[["nʌt","nʌt"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研"],[["原形","nut"],["现在分词","nutting"],["过去式","nutted"],["过去分词","nutted"],["形容词","nutlike",1],["名词","nutter",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","坚果",0],["n.","螺母；螺帽",0],["n.","人的头（或大脑）",0],["n.","怪人；疯子",0],["n.","着迷的人；专注于某事的人；…迷",0],["n.","睾丸",0],["v.","（故意）以头撞击",0]],[],"nut.mp3",null],"nutrition":[["njuːˈtrɪʃ.ᵊn","nuˈtrɪʃ·ən"],["高中","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS","GRE"],[["复数","nutritions"],["形容词","nutritional",1],["副词","nutritionally",1]],[4,1.5,4,2,1],[["n.","营养；滋养；营养的补给",4]],[["2016 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","It is like the immune system of the body, which under stress or through lack of nutrition or exercise can be weakened, but which never leaves us.","它就像人体的免疫系统：压力、营养不足或缺乏锻炼会使它减弱，但它从不会离我们而去。","正文"],["2008 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","At the start of the 20th century, under-nutrition and childhood infections got in the way.","20世纪初，营养不良和儿童期感染阻碍了生长。","正文"],["2019 英二 · 完形","I use my bimonthly weigh-in results to get information about my nutrition as well.","我也利用每两周一次的称重结果了解自己的营养摄入情况。",""]],"nutrition.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nutrit-,nutri- = nourish, 表示“营养”。"],["后缀","-ion,-ation,-ition 表名词，“行为、动作、状态、过程、结果；物品”等。"]],"d":[["malnutrition","n. 营养失调，营养不良"],["denutrition","n. 营养缺乏；营养不良"],["innutrition","n. 营养不良"],["nutritional","营养"],["nutritionist","n. 营养学家"]]}],"napkin":[["ˈnæp.kɪn","ˈnæp·kɪn"],["CET6","考研"],[["复数","napkins"]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","餐巾；餐巾纸",0]],[],"napkin.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nap- 表示“桌布”，来自古法语nape桌布。"],["后缀","-kin 表名词，“小…”，源自低地德语 -ken, 和德语后缀 -chen 同源。"]],"d":[]}],"neck":[["nek","nek"],["中考","高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["复数","necks"],["原形","neck"],["第三人称单数","necks"],["现在分词","necking"],["过去式","necked"],["过去分词","necked"],["形容词","neckless",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","颈；脖子",0],["n.","衣领；领子；领圈",0],["n.","有…衣领的；有…脖子的",0],["n.","（物体的）细长部分，颈部",0],["n.","（烹制食用的）动物颈肉",0],["v.","搂着脖子亲吻；相拥互吻",0]],[],"neck.mp3",null],"neighbor":[["ˈneɪ.bəʳ","ˈneɪ·bər"],["考研","TOEFL"],[["复数","neighbors"],["原形","neighbor"],["第三人称单数","neighbors"],["现在分词","neighboring"],["过去式","neighbored"],["过去分词","neighbored"],["形容词","neighborless",1]],[5,2.0,2,3,2],[["n.","邻居；邻人",1],["n.","邻国",0],["n.","身边的人；靠近的东西；邻近的人（或物）",1],["n.","他人；世人",0],["v.","与…相邻；邻近",3]],[["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","It is too easy, and misleading, to see such court rulings as merely standing up for the rights of land owners when the consequences can be so dire for their neighbors.","如果后果可能给邻居带来如此严重的危害，却只把这类法院裁决看作维护土地所有者的权利，那就既轻率又误导人。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","And it’s a reminder that the EPA’s involvement in the Chesapeake Bay Program has long been crucial as the means to transcend the influence of deep-pocketed special interests in neighboring states.","这也提醒我们，环保署长期参与切萨皮克湾计划至关重要，因为它使保护工作得以摆脱邻州财力雄厚的特殊利益集团的影响。","正文"],["2011 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","The apartments in the elegant towers Mies built on Chicago’s Lake Shore Drive, for example, were smaller — two-bedroom units under 1,000 square feet — than those in their older neighbors along the city’s Gold Coast.","例如，密斯在芝加哥湖滨大道建造的雅致高层住宅中，公寓面积比该市黄金海岸沿线较老建筑里的公寓更小：两居室不足1000平方英尺。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4 · 第39题 · 选项A","What can be inferred about the EPA’s involvement in the Chesapeake Bay Program? It has restored the balance among neighboring jurisdictions.","关于美国环保署参与切萨皮克湾计划，可以推断出什么？它恢复了相邻辖区之间的平衡。","选项"],["2011 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3 · 第34题 · 选项C","What is true about the apartments Mies built on Chicago’s Lake Shore Drive? They were more spacious than neighboring buildings.","关于密斯在芝加哥湖滨大道建造的公寓，哪一项说法属实？它们比邻近的建筑更加宽敞。","选项"]],"neighbor.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neigh- = near, 表示“附近”。"],["后缀","-or 表示“人或物”，是施动者名词。是拉丁语后缀 -tor 的俗化（可能受英语本土后缀 -er 的影响）形式。"]],"d":[["neighborhood","n. 地区;某地区的人;与某处邻近的地区"],["neighborly","睦邻的"],["neighboring","邻近"],["neighborless","adj. 无邻居的,孤独的"],["neighborwise","邻向"]]}],"neither":[["ˈnaɪ.ðəʳ","ˈni·ðər"],["中考","高中"],[],[7,2.0,6,4,0],[["determiner, pronoun","两者都不",4],["adv.","（否定的陈述同样适用于其他人或物）也不",0],["adv.","（否定的陈述适用于两方面）既不…也不…",3]],[["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","Neither one of them actually participated in any contributions to animal research or conservation.","实际上，这两家机构都未为动物研究或保护工作作出任何贡献。","正文"],["2016 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Looking back, he is struck that his parents could provide a comfortable life for their children even though neither had completed college when he was young.","回想过去，他惊讶地发现，在他小时候，父母虽然都没读完大学，却能让孩子过上舒适的生活。","正文"],["2012 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","Neither of these patterns is borne out by the analysis, suggesting that the structures of the languages are lineage-specific and not governed by universals.","分析结果并未证实这两种模式中的任何一种，这表明语言结构因谱系而异，并非由普遍规律支配。","正文"],["2006 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Writing for the National Immigration Forum, Gregory Rodriguez reports that today’s immigration is neither at unprecedented levels nor resistant to assimilation.","格雷戈里·罗德里格斯为全国移民论坛撰文指出，如今的移民规模既未达到空前水平，移民也并非抗拒同化。","正文"],["2023 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3 · 第35题 · 选项B","Neither Sparrow nor Storm would agree that the Internet is weakening our memory.","斯帕罗和斯托姆都不会认同“互联网正在削弱我们的记忆力”这一说法。","题干"],["2019 英一 · 阅读 · Part B · 选项G","If you yell, “Yes,” and I yell, “No,” neither of us learns anything.","如果你喊“是”，我喊“不”，我们谁也学不到东西。",""]],"neither.mp3",{"r":[["后缀","-er 是施动者名词后缀，表示“人或物”，一般缀于动词后，来自古英语。"]],"d":[]}],"nephew":[["ˈnef.juː","ˈnef·ju"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研"],[["复数","nephews"]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","侄子；外甥",0]],[],"nephew.mp3",null],"nickel":[["ˈnɪk.ᵊl","ˈnɪk·əl"],["CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["复数","nickels"],["形容词","nickelous",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","镍",0],["n.","（美国和加拿大的）5 分镍币",0]],[],"nickel.mp3",null],"nitrogen":[["ˈnaɪ.trə.dʒən","ˈnɑɪ·trə·dʒən"],["CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["复数","nitrogens"],["形容词","nitrogenous",1]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["n.","氮；氮气",1]],[["2010 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","Nitrogen-oxide emissions during the cruising portions of the flight fell by around a quarter.","飞行巡航阶段的氮氧化物排放量下降了约四分之一。","正文"]],"nitrogen.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nitr- = niter, nitrogen. 表示“硝基; 氮”。氮最早是在研究硝石的时候认识的。nitroso- 表示亚硝基。"],["词根","gen-,gener-,genit-,-genesis = birth, produce, 表示“出生，产生”，医学上引申为“生殖或基因”。"]],"d":[["dinitrogen","二氮"],["nitrogenase","固氮"],["nitrogenous","adj. 氮的,含氮的"],["amidonitrogen","酰胺态氮"],["radionitrogen","放射性氮"]]}],"niece":[["niːs","nis"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研"],[["复数","nieces"],["形容词","nieceless",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","侄女；外甥女",0]],[],"niece.mp3",null],"nobody":[["ˈnəʊ.bə.di","ˈnoʊ·bə·di"],["中考","高中"],[["复数","nobodies"]],[4,1.5,3,2,0],[["pron.","小人物；无足轻重的人",0],["n.","小人物；无足轻重的人",0],["pron.","没有人，无人",4]],[["2012 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","But thinking what nobody else has thought and telling others what they have missed may not change their views.","但想到别人未曾想到的事，再告诉他们自己忽略了什么，未必能改变他们的看法。","正文"],["2012 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Nobel Laureate and physiologist Albert Szent-Gyorgyi once described discovery as “seeing what everybody has seen and thinking what nobody has thought.”","诺贝尔奖得主、生理学家阿尔伯特·圣捷尔吉曾这样描述发现：“看到人人都看到的东西，却想到无人想到的事情。”","正文"],["2025 英二 · 完形","Nobody knows everything and can do everything all by themselves.","没有人无所不知，也没有人能独自完成一切。",""],["2020 英二 · 完形","And then the inevitable happens: You lose your patience and either scream at your kids or say something that was too harsh and does nobody any good.","接着不可避免的事发生了：你失去耐心，冲孩子大喊大叫，或者说出过于严厉、对谁都没有好处的话。",""]],"nobody.mp3",{"r":[["词根","body- = body, 表示“身体”。"]],"d":[]}],"nod":[["nɒd","nɑd"],["中考","高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL"],[["复数","nods"],["原形","nod"],["第三人称单数","nods"],["现在分词","nodding"],["过去式","nodded"],["过去分词","nodded"],["名词","nodder",1]],[2,1.0,2,2,0],[["v.","点头",1],["v.","点头致意；点头示意",0],["v.","（朝…方向）点头（表示所谈论的人或物）",0],["v.","打盹；打瞌睡",0],["n.","点头",0],["n.","被选中；得到许可",1]],[["2011 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","As boards scrutinize succession plans in response to shareholder pressure, executives who don't get the nod also may wish to move on.","在股东压力下，董事会开始仔细审视接班计划；未获选中的高管也可能想另谋出路。","正文"],["2010 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","This man quickly nodded in agreement.","这名男子立刻点头表示赞同。","正文"]],"nod.mp3",null],"noisy":[["ˈnɔɪ.zi","ˈnɔɪ.zi"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["比较级","noisier"],["最高级","noisiest"],["副词","noisily",1],["名词","noisiness",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["adj.","吵闹的；聒噪的；嘈杂的",0],["adj.","充满噪音的；吵吵闹闹的",0]],[],"noisy.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nav-,naus-,naut- = ship, 表示“船”，naut- 引申为“海员”。"],["后缀","-y 表形容词，加在名词后变成形容词。"]],"d":[["noisily","adv. 吵闹地，喧闹地"],["noisiness","吵闹"]]}],"nor":[["nɔːʳ","nɔr；nər"],["中考","高中"],[],[10,2.5,9,8,0],[["conjunction, adverb","也不",6],["conjunction, adverb","（用于肯定动词前，表示同意刚提及的否定命题）也不",3],["conj., adv.","也不",1]],[["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Nor should their work be considered only as an object of study.","他们的作品也不应仅仅被视为研究对象。","正文"],["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Nor are highly paid managers themselves immune from the harm caused by the ERA’s unjustified dismissal procedures.","高薪经理本人也不能免受《雇佣关系法》中不合理解雇程序造成的伤害。","正文"],["2016 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Nor does it reveal how much companies are banking on the halo effect, rather than the other possible benefits, when they decide their do-gooding policies.","研究也没有揭示，公司在制定行善政策时，有多大程度是寄望于光环效应，而不是其他潜在好处。","正文"],["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Ms Brooks may or may not have had suspicions about how her journalists got their stories, but she asked no questions, gave no instructions — nor received traceable, recorded answers.","布鲁克斯女士对记者如何获得报道可能有所怀疑，也可能毫无察觉，但她没有提问、没有作出指示，也没有收到可追溯、有记录的答复。","正文"],["2014 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Nor was there any evidence that those who self-enhanced the most (that is, the participants who thought the most positively doctored pictures were real) were doing so to make up for profound insecurities.","也没有证据表明，那些自我美化程度最高的人——即认为修饰得最漂亮的照片才是真实照片的参与者——这样做是为了弥补深层的不安全感。","正文"],["2012 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","For them, history did nothing, it possessed no immense wealth nor waged battles: “It is man, real, living man who does all that.”","在他们看来，历史本身什么也不做；它既不拥有巨大的财富，也不进行战争：“做到这一切的是人，是现实的、活生生的人。”","正文"]],"nor.mp3",null],"northwest":[["ˌnɔːθˈwest","ˌnɔrθˈwest"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研"],[["复数","northwests"]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","西北向，西北方",0],["adj. / adv.","在西北的;向西北的",0]],[],"northwest.mp3",{"r":[["词根","hesp-,vesp-,west 希腊语 hesperos 和拉丁语 vesper, \"evening, west\"，表示“黄昏”。英语中 west 和其同源。源自印欧词根 *wes-。"]],"d":[]}],"nose":[["nəʊz","noʊz"],["中考","高中"],[["复数","noses"],["原形","nose"],["第三人称单数","noses"],["现在分词","nosing"],["过去式","nosed"],["过去分词","nosed"],["形容词","noseless",1],["名词","noser",1],["副词","noselessly",1],["名词","noselessness",1]],[6,2.0,3,1,0],[["n.","鼻；鼻子",6],["n.","有…鼻子的",0],["n.","（飞机、太空船等的）头部，头锥；机头",0],["n.","发现（或辨别）事物的能力；嗅觉",0],["n.","嗅觉",0],["n.","特有的气味",0],["v.","小心翼翼地向前移动",0],["v.","（用鼻子）嗅，拱，顶",0]],[["2017 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","But it did so while holding its nose at the ethics of his conduct, which included accepting gifts such as a Rolex watch and a Ferrari automobile from a company seeking access to government.","但法院作出这一裁决时，对他的行为操守深感反感，其中包括接受一家试图接近政府官员的公司赠送的劳力士手表、法拉利汽车等礼物。","正文"],["2018 英一 · 完形","Scientists have found that exposure to this hormone puts us in a trusting mood : In a Swiss study, researchers sprayed oxytocin into the noses of half the subjects; those subjects were ready to lend significantly higher amounts of money to strangers than were their counterparts who inhaled something else.","科学家发现，接触这种激素会让人更愿意信任他人：在瑞士的一项研究中，研究人员向一半受试者的鼻腔喷入催产素；与吸入其他物质的受试者相比，他们愿意借给陌生人的金额明显更高。",""],["2005 英一 · 完形","The human nose is an underrated tool.","人的鼻子是一种被低估的感官工具。",""],["2005 英一 · 完形","Our noses are capable of detecting human smells even when these are diluted to far below one part in one million.","即使人体气味被稀释到远低于百万分之一的浓度，我们的鼻子仍能察觉到它。",""],["2005 英一 · 完形","This may be because some people do not have the genes necessary to generate particular smell receptors in the nose.","这可能是因为有些人缺少在鼻内生成某些特定嗅觉感受器所必需的基因。",""],["2005 英一 · 完形","This means that our noses are limited to perceiving those smells which float through the air, missing the majority of smells which stick to surfaces.","这意味着我们的鼻子只能闻到飘浮在空气中的气味，却闻不到附着在物体表面的绝大多数气味。",""]],"nose.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nas-,naso- = nose, 表示“鼻”。 nas- 来自拉丁语，nos- 来自古英语，他们都源自原始印欧语 *nas-。"]],"d":[["nostril","n. 鼻孔"],["nozzle","n. 喷嘴；管口；鼻"],["nosy","adj. 好管闲事的；爱追问的；大鼻子的"],["nosegay","n. 花束"],["nosed","1. adj. 有…鼻子的 2. v. 嗅；侦察出（nose的过去分词）"]]}],"noun":[["naʊn","nɑʊn"],["CET4","CET6","考研"],[["复数","nouns"],["形容词","nounal",1],["副词","nounally",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","名词",0]],[],"noun.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nom-,nomin-,nam- = name, 表示“名称，名字”。"]],"d":[["pronoun","n. [语]代词"]]}],"nurse":[["nɜːs","nɜrs"],["中考","高中","TOEFL","IELTS"],[["复数","nurses"],["原形","nurse"],["第三人称单数","nurses"],["现在分词","nursing"],["过去式","nursed"],["过去分词","nursed"],["名词","nurser",1]],[5,2.0,4,4,0],[["n.","护士",4],["n.","（旧时雇主家中的）女保育员，保姆，女仆",0],["v.","看护，照料（病人或伤者）",1],["v.","调治，调养（伤病）",0],["v.","怀抱；怀有；心藏",0],["v.","培育；培养；悉心照料",0],["v.","搂抱；小心抱着",0],["v.","喂奶；哺育",0],["v.","吃奶；吸奶",0]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Many have nurses on site to carry out basic health checks, with a link to the GP’s surgery.","许多图书馆还有护士驻点开展基本健康检查，并与全科诊所衔接。","正文"],["2021 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","In the medical field, to take an obvious example, the pandemic meant that there were still clear shortages of doctors, nurses and other medical personnel.","举一个明显的例子：在医疗领域，疫情意味着医生、护士和其他医务人员仍然明显短缺。","正文"],["2017 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","At Boston College, for example, you would have to complete an extra year were you to switch to the nursing school from another department.","例如，在波士顿学院，如果从其他院系转入护理学院，就得额外读一年。","正文"],["2002 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Here is an example, which I heard at a nurses’ convention, of a story which works well because the audience all shared the same view of doctors.","我在一次护士大会上听过这样一个笑话；它很奏效，因为听众对医生都抱有相同的看法。","正文"],["2002 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1 · 第22题 · 选项B","The joke about doctors implies that, in the eyes of nurses, they are very conscious of their godlike role.","关于医生的笑话暗示，在护士眼中，他们是十分在意自己如神一般的地位的。","题干"]],"nurse.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nour-,nurs- 表示“喂养，营养”。"]],"d":[["nursery","n. 托儿所；苗圃；温床"],["nurser","n. 培育者；奶瓶；奶妈"],["nursing","1. n. 护理；养育；看护 2. v. 看护；养育（nurse的ing形式）"],["nursling","n. 被精心培育的东西；婴儿"],["day-nurse","日班护士"]]}],"nylon":[["ˈnaɪ.lɒn","ˈnɑɪ·lɑn"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[["复数","nylons"]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","尼龙",0],["n.","（女用）尼龙长袜，尼龙连袜裤",0]],[],"nylon.mp3",null],"name":[["neɪm","neɪm"],["中考","高中"],[["复数","names"],["原形","name"],["第三人称单数","names"],["现在分词","naming"],["过去式","named"],["过去分词","named"],["名词","namer",1],["形容词","nameless",1],["副词","namelessly",1],["名词","namelessness",1]],[77,4.5,42,21,3],[["n.","名字；名称",67],["n.","名誉；名声；名气",2],["n.","有…名称的；以…著名的；有…名声的",1],["n.","名人",0],["v.","命名；给…取名",2],["v.","说出…的名称；叫出…的名字",4],["v.","确定；说定；准确陈述",0],["v.","任命；委任",1]],[["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","The online search brought back work that had his name attached to it but wasn’t his.","网上搜索却找出了署着他的名字、并非出自他之手的作品。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Then he tried searching for his name to see if a piece he had worked on had been published.","后来他试着搜索自己的名字，想看看自己创作的作品是否发表了。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","According to the website Lexica, which tracks over 10 million images and prompts generated by Stable Diffusion, Rutkowski’s name has been used as a prompt around 93,000 times.","Lexica网站追踪了Stable Diffusion生成的一千多万张图像及其提示词；据该网站统计，鲁特科夫斯基的名字被用作提示词约九万三千次。","正文"],["2023 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Big-name PRH authors may suffer a bit, but it’s those mid-list authors, who normally rely on Waterstones staff’s passion for promoting books by lesser-known writers, who will be praying for an end to the dispute.","该社的知名作者可能受到些许影响，但真正盼望这场争端结束的，是那些处于中游的作者：他们通常依靠水石书店员工的热情，来推广不太知名作家的作品。","正文"],["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","The founders deliberately focused their projects around light — hence the “visual studies” in the name.","创办者有意让项目围绕光展开，因此中心名称中有了“视觉研究”一词。","正文"],["2020 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","These have included Britain’s DPT (diverted profits tax), Australia’s MAAL (multinational antiavoidance law), and India’s SEP (significant economic presence) test, to name but a few.","其中包括英国的DPT（转移利润税）、澳大利亚的MAAL（跨国企业反避税法），以及印度的SEP（显著经济存在）测试，这只是几个例子。","正文"]],"name.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nom-,nomin-,nam- = name, 表示“名称，名字”。"]],"d":[["surname","1. n. 姓，姓氏；绰号，别名 2. vt. 给…起别名；给…姓氏"],["namely","adv. 即是；也就是；换句话说"],["nickname","1. n. 绰号；昵称 2. vt. 给……取绰号；叫错名字"],["namesake","n. 名义；同名物；同名的人"],["named","1. adj. 被指名的；命名的；指定的 2. v. 命名；称呼；任命（name的过去分词）"]]}],"near":[["nɪəʳ","nɪər"],["中考","高中"],[["原形","near"],["第三人称单数","nears"],["现在分词","nearing"],["过去式","neared"],["过去分词","neared"],["比较级","nearer"],["最高级","nearest"],["名词","nearness",1]],[18,3.0,15,12,0],[["prep.","在…附近；靠近",5],["prep.","接近；临近",0],["prep.","（用于数词前）大约，上下，接近",0],["prep.","（质量、大小等）相仿，接近",0],["prep.","接近于（某种状态）；濒临；快要",2],["adj.","距离近；不远",3],["adj.","不久以后",5],["adj.","随后；接近",0],["adj.","近似；相似；不分伯仲",0],["adj.","接近的；差不多的",2],["adj.","（亲属关系）近亲",0],["adv.","距离不远；在附近",0],["adv.","不久以后",0],["adv.","几乎；差不多",0],["v.","（时间或空间上）接近，靠近，临近",0],["adj.","至亲；至爱；最亲密的亲友",1]],[["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","As demand for healthcare continues to grow, pressures on the workforce — which is already near breaking point — will only become more acute.","随着医疗需求持续增长，本已接近崩溃边缘的医护队伍将承受更加严峻的压力。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","What is more, they almost always seem to choose the nearest waterhole.","而且，它们似乎几乎总会选择最近的水潭。","正文"],["2023 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","If you’re heading for your nearest branch of Waterstones, the biggest book retailer in the UK, in search of the Duchess of Sussex’s new children’s book The Bench, you might have to be prepared to hunt around a bit; the same may be true of The President’s Daughter, the new thriller by Bill Clinton and James Patterson.","如果你去英国最大的图书零售商水石书店离你最近的分店，寻找萨塞克斯公爵夫人的新童书《长凳》，可能得做好四处寻觅的准备；比尔·克林顿与詹姆斯·帕特森合著的新惊悚小说《总统的女儿》也可能如此。","正文"],["2015 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","Try to keep in mind that almost everyone respects and wants to help you if you are trying to make a good change in your life, especially your dearest and nearest people.","请记住，只要你努力让生活向好的方向改变，几乎每个人都会尊重你、愿意帮助你，尤其是你最亲近的人。","正文"],["2013 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","That’s one reason why we have launched Arc, a new publication dedicated to the near future.","这也是我们创办《Arc》的一个原因；这是一份关注不久将来的新刊物。","正文"],["2011 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","A year ago the end seemed near.","一年前，报纸的末日似乎近在眼前。","正文"]],"near.mp3",null],"need":[["niːd","nid"],["中考","高中"],[["原形","need"],["第三人称单数","needs"],["第三人称单数","need or (auxiliary)"],["现在分词","needing"],["过去式","needed"],["过去分词","needed"],["形容词","needful",1],["副词","needfully",1],["名词","needfulness",1],["形容词","unneedful",1]],[295,5.0,44,174,35],[["v.","需要；必需",97],["v.","（表示应该或不得不做）有必要",113],["n.","需要；必须",34],["n.","特别需要；迫切要求",8],["n.","需要的事物；欲望",38],["n.","（食物、钱或生活来源的）短缺，缺乏",4],["modal v.","（表示没有必要或询问是否有必要）需要",1]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","People need to be ready.","人们必须提前做好准备。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Employers need to manage AI tools with the same level of care as any other form of data sharing or storage.","雇主需要像管理其他形式的数据共享或存储一样，审慎管理人工智能工具。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","Their interests as stewards of the land need to be better integrated with those who have the money to support restoration.","作为土地管理者，农民的关切需要与出资支持生态恢复者的关切更好地结合起来。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","To prevent entire ecosystems from going up in smoke, Martin said, people must bring healthy fire back to places that need it.","马丁说，为防止整个生态系统毁于火灾，人们必须让有益的火重新回到需要它的地方。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","There’s no need to back away from progress, as long as we’re equipped with the knowledge and tools to make sure AI remains a friend.","只要我们掌握足够的知识和工具，确保人工智能始终是我们的朋友，就没有必要拒绝进步。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","There’s also a knowledge gap that needs to be addressed — 40% of individuals surveyed are unsure about who retains ownership over the content produced by AI.","还有一项知识缺口需要填补：在受访者中，40% 不确定人工智能生成内容的所有权归谁。","正文"]],"need.mp3",null],"never":[["ˈnev.əʳ","ˈnev·ər"],["中考","高中"],[],[49,4.0,29,36,2],[["adv.","从不；绝不；从未；未曾",43],["adv.","（与 not 同义，语气较强）一点都不，从未",6],["exclam.","（表示惊讶，因为觉得不可能）不会吧",0]],[["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Production has been slipping away from Hollywood since the 1950s, but the effects have never been more apparent than at present.","自20世纪50年代以来，影视制作一直在离开好莱坞，而这种变化的影响从未像现在这样明显。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","I loved the man from the Thirties research who found that wireless suddenly offered “a lot of variety...things I thought I’d never be interested in...ice hockey perhaps”.","我很喜欢30年代那项研究中的一名受访男子。他发现，无线广播突然带来了“许多不同的内容……有些东西我原以为自己绝不会感兴趣……比如冰球”。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","There will be no charge and you will never be asked to justify or explain yourself; you will simply be welcomed in, offered help if you need it, and left alone if you do not.","这里不收费，也绝不会要求你为到访说明理由；你只会受到欢迎，需要帮助时有人相助，不需要时也不会有人打扰。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","Although these efforts were aimed at the nonscience-bound student, they never really made their way into mainstream thought and public discourse as a means to rally widespread support for the importance of science teaching in schools.","尽管这些努力面向不打算从事科学工作的学生，但它们作为争取广泛支持学校科学教学重要性的手段，始终没有真正进入主流思想和公共讨论。","正文"],["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Ever since taking on Netflix Inc. at its own game, old Hollywood has struggled to turn a profit in streaming, with the likes of Disney+, Peacock and Paramount+ losing billions of dollars each year, sparking concerns that the services will never be as profitable as cable once was.","自从与奈飞公司在流媒体领域正面交锋以来，传统好莱坞一直难以从流媒体业务中获利。迪士尼+、Peacock和Paramount+等服务每年亏损数十亿美元，引发人们担忧：这些服务或许永远无法像曾经的有线电视那样赚钱。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","“Elephants never forget” — or so they say — and that piece of folklore seems to have some foundation.","“大象永远不会忘记”——人们常这样说，而这句民间说法似乎确有几分根据。","正文"]],"never.mp3",null],"news":[["njuːz","nuz"],["中考","高中"],[["复数","newses"],["形容词","newsless",1],["形容词","newsy",1],["名词","newsiness",1]],[38,4.0,14,29,4],[["n.","消息；音信",6],["n.","媒体对重要事情的报道；新闻",30],["n.","（电视或广播中的）新闻报道",2],["n.","新闻人物；新闻事件",0]],[["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Though it’s still unclear why the original domestication happened, Science News’ Freda Kreier reports that the event coincided with the Sahara growing larger and drier.","《科学新闻》的弗雷达·克赖尔报道说，虽然最初为何驯化驴仍不清楚，但这件事恰逢撒哈拉沙漠范围扩大、气候变得更加干燥。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","In my own book about radio I recorded how, on one drive: “I caught up with the news, learnt some 17th-century history, and was startlingly educated by an unpretentious programme on the history of the stethoscope.”","在我自己写的广播著作中，我记下一次开车时的经历：“我了解了最新消息，学到一些17世纪的历史知识，还被一档讲述听诊器历史的朴实节目意外地上了一课。”","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","In Maryland, the good news is that there are many state laws in place that provide wetlands protections.","好消息是，马里兰州已有许多州法保护湿地。","正文"],["2019 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","\"That's good news,\" Malti says.","“这是个好消息，”马尔蒂说。","正文"],["2018 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","In other words, the choice to share news on social media may be the heart of the issue.","换句话说，选择在社交媒体上分享新闻，可能正是问题的核心。","正文"],["2018 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","They cross-check sources and prefer news from different perspectives — especially those that are open about any bias.","他们交叉核对消息来源，更青睐从不同视角报道的新闻，尤其是公开承认自身偏见的报道。","正文"]],"news.mp3",null],"newspaper":[["ˈnjuːzˌpeɪ.pəʳ","ˈnuzˌpeɪ·pər"],["中考","高中","IELTS"],[["复数","newspapers"],["原形","newspaper"],["第三人称单数","newspapers"],["现在分词","newspapering"],["过去式","newspapered"],["过去分词","newspapered"],["形容词","newspaperish",1]],[54,4.5,11,20,12],[["n.","报纸；报",54],["n.","旧报纸",0]],[["2016 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","The infrastructure required to make a physical newspaper — printing presses, delivery trucks — isn’t just expensive; it’s excessive at a time when online-only competitors don’t have the same set of financial constraints.","制作实体报纸所需的基础设施——印刷机、送报卡车——不仅昂贵，而且在纯网络竞争者无需承担同样财务负担的今天显得多余。","正文"],["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","The words that have mattered are efficiency, flexibility, shareholder value, business-friendly, wealth generation, sales, impact and, in newspapers, circulation.","被看重的词语是效率、灵活性、股东价值、亲商、创造财富、销售额、影响力，以及对报纸而言的发行量。","正文"],["2011 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Newspapers are less complete as a result.","因此，报纸的内容不再那么全面。","正文"],["2011 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Whatever happened to the death of newspapers?","报纸之死后来怎么样了？","正文"],["2011 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Not surprisingly, Japanese newspapers are much more stable.","因此，日本报纸稳定得多，也就不足为奇了。","正文"],["2011 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","But completeness is no longer a virtue in the newspaper business.","但在报业，内容全面已不再是一种优势。","正文"]],"newspaper.mp3",{"r":[["词根","paper-,papyr- 表示“草纸”，埃及语经由拉丁语进入英语。"]],"d":[["newspaperman","n. 报社记者;新闻编辑"]]}],"next":[["nekst","nekst"],["中考","高中"],[["副词","nextly",1]],[49,4.0,30,40,0],[["adj.","下一个的；紧接着的；接下来的",27],["adj.","紧随其后的；下一个的",13],["adv.","紧接着；随后",4],["adv.","其次的；依次的；仅次于…的",0],["adv.","（用于询问，表示吃惊或困惑）",0],["n.","下一位；下一个；下一件",3],["adj., pron.","下一个的；其次的；紧接着的",1],["adv.","接近，几乎",1]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Ferrovie will invest a total of €124bn in infrastructure over the next 10 years.","意大利国家铁路集团将在未来十年投入总计 1,240 亿欧元改善基础设施。","正文"],["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Consulting firm Parks Associates predicts that legitimate US streaming services’ cumulative loss from piracy since 2022 will reach $113 billion in the next two years.","咨询公司帕克斯联合公司预测，2022年以来美国合法流媒体服务因盗版遭受的累计损失，将在未来两年达到1130亿美元。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Pennsylvania farmers, to use one telling example, aren’t thinking about next year’s blue crab harvest in Maryland when they decide whether to spread animal waste on their fields, yet the runoff into nearby creeks can have enormous impact downstream.","举一个很能说明问题的例子：宾夕法尼亚州的农民决定是否把牲畜粪便撒在田里时，不会想着马里兰州明年的蓝蟹收成；然而，流入附近溪流的地表径流可能对下游造成巨大影响。","正文"],["2023 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Both of these books are published next week by Penguin Random House (PRH), a company currently involved in a stand-off with Waterstones.","这两本书都将于下周由企鹅兰登书屋出版，而这家公司目前与水石书店陷入僵局。","正文"],["2023 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","Some 81% of respondents said they would be willing to pay additional taxes for the next 10 years to avoid any cuts to the national parks.","约81%的受访者表示，他们愿意在未来10年多缴税，以避免国家公园的经费遭到任何削减。","正文"],["2023 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","Any plans submitted before that date are considered to be under the previous rules, and can go ahead as long as work starts before 15th June next year.","在该日期之前提交的任何规划，都按旧规处理；只要工程在明年6月15日之前开工，就可以继续进行。","正文"]],"next.mp3",null],"nice":[["naɪs","nɑɪs"],["中考","高中","GRE"],[["比较级","nicer"],["最高级","nicest"],["副词","nicely",1],["名词","niceness",1]],[3,1.5,3,1,1],[["adj.","令人愉快的；宜人的；吸引人的",3],["adj.","（用于形容词或副词前以加强语气）",0],["adj.","好心的；和蔼的；友好的",0],["adj.","坏的；令人不愉快的",0],["adj.","细微的；精细的",0]],[["2020 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","This will help to grow your internal network, in addition to being a nice break in the work day.","除了是工作日里一次愉快的休息之外，这也有助于扩大你在公司内部的人脉。","正文"],["2023 英二 · 完形","Here’s a common scenario that any number of entrepreneurs face today: you’re the CEO of a small business, and though you’re making a nice profit, you need to find a way to take it to the next level.","如今，许多创业者都面临这样一种常见情况：你是一家小企业的首席执行官，虽然利润不错，但你需要找到办法，让企业更上一层楼。",""],["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1 · 第23题 · 选项C","Female capuchin monkeys were chosen for the research most probably because they are nice in both appearance and temperament.","研究选择雌性卷尾猴，很可能是因为它们外表漂亮，性情温和。","选项"]],"nice.mp3",{"r":[["词根","sci- = know, 表示“知道”，sci-最初表示to cut“切”。引申为 \"know how to cut\" 即“知道”。"],["前缀","un- 表示“不，无，非，没有”。"]],"d":[["nicety","n. 美好；精密；细节；拘泥细节"],["nicely","adv. 恰好地；漂亮地；精细地"],["overnice","adj. 过分讲究的；过于吹毛求疵的；过份洁癖的"],["nice-looking","好看的"]]}],"night":[["naɪt","nɑɪt"],["中考","高中","IELTS"],[["复数","nights"],["形容词","nightless",1],["副词","nightly",1]],[14,3.0,6,8,0],[["n.","夜；夜晚",14],["n.","晚上，夜晚（夜里就寝前的一段时间）",0],["n.","（举行盛事的）夜晚；…之夜",0]],[["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Without constant migration of digital assets, a nightmare about the foreseeable future is what keeps historians up at night: a historical record that abruptly stops when digital replace analog.","如果不持续迁移数字资产，历史学家便会被一个可预见的未来噩梦弄得夜不能寐：数字媒介取代模拟媒介之后，历史记录突然中断。","正文"],["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","As a librarian whose day job revolves around special collections and digital assets, I share the night terrors of historians, and I’d be lying if I said a comprehensive preservation solution currently exists.","作为一名日常工作围绕特藏与数字资产展开的图书馆员，我和历史学家一样会为此做噩梦；如果说目前已经有全面的保存方案，那就是在撒谎。","正文"],["2006 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","He sometimes played two slot machines at a time, all night, until the boat docked at 5 a.m., then went back aboard when the casino opened at 9 a.m.","他有时整晚同时玩两台老虎机，直到凌晨5点赌船靠岸；等赌场上午9点开门，他又返回船上。","正文"],["2006 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","It is the playgoers, the RSC contends, who bring in much of the town’s revenue because they spend the night (some of them four or five nights) pouring cash into the hotels and restaurants.","皇家莎士比亚剧团认为，为小镇带来大部分收入的正是看戏的人，因为他们会留宿（有些人住四五晚），在旅馆和餐馆花大把的钱。","正文"],["2006 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","They all seem to look alike (though they come from all over) — lean, pointed, dedicated faces, wearing jeans and sandals, eating their buns and bedding down for the night on the flagstones outside the theatre to buy the 20 seats and 80 standing-room tickets held for the sleepers and sold to them when the box office opens at 10:30 a.m.","他们虽然来自四面八方，却看起来都差不多——身材清瘦，脸庞尖削，神情专注；穿着牛仔裤和凉鞋，吃着面包卷，夜里就睡在剧院外的石板地上，为的是买到留给这些露宿者、在上午10点半售票处开门时出售的20张座位票和80张站票。","正文"],["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Of all the components of a good night’s sleep, dreams seem to be least within our control.","在优质睡眠的各个组成部分中，梦似乎最不受我们控制。","正文"]],"night.mp3",{"r":[["词根","noct-,nyct-,night = night, 表示“夜晚”。 noct- 源自拉丁语，nyct- 源自希腊语，night 源自古英语（日耳曼语），他们都来源于原始印欧语 *nekwt- (night)。"]],"d":[["tonight","1. adv. 在今晚 2. n. 今晚"],["fortnight","n. 两星期, 十四天"],["overnight","在夜间；突然；一夜之间;突然, 很快"],["midnight","1. n. 午夜，半夜12点钟 2. adj. 半夜的；漆黑的"],["nightmare","n. 噩梦 〈口〉可怕的事情, 无法摆脱的恐惧"]]}],"nine":[["naɪn","nɑɪn"],["中考","高中"],[["复数","nines"]],[6,2.0,6,5,0],[["num.","九",6]],[["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","The randomised control trial involved hundreds of year 5 pupils — aged nine and ten — at 45 state primary schools that had not been “previously exposed to RSC pedagogy.”","这项随机对照试验涉及45所公立小学的数百名五年级学生，他们年龄为九岁和十岁；此前这些学校未接触过“皇家莎士比亚剧团教学法”。","正文"],["2022 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","If you were walking 3 miles a day, playing 18 holes of golf three times a week, or lifting 10-pound dumbbells for three sets of 10 reps, reduce activity to half a mile every other day, or nine holes of golf once a week with short walks on other days, or use 5-pound dumbbells for one set of 10 reps.","如果以前你每天步行3英里、每周打三次18洞高尔夫，或用10磅哑铃做三组、每组10次，那么现在就改为隔天步行半英里，或每周打一次9洞高尔夫、其他日子短距离散步，或用5磅哑铃只做一组10次。","正文"],["2021 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Another set of participants had to count backward from 1,000 by nines as they watched the clips, occupying their conscious working memory.","另一组参与者观看视频时必须从1000开始每次减9倒数，这占用了他们有意识的工作记忆。","正文"],["2016 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","A couple of Christmases ago, my youngest stepdaughter, who was nine years old at the time, got a Superman T-shirt for Christmas.","两年前的圣诞节，我当时九岁、年龄最小的继女收到了一件超人T恤作为圣诞礼物。","正文"],["2008 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","So he hired a dentist to transplant nine teeth into his jaw — having extracted them from the mouths of his slaves.","于是他雇了一名牙医，将九颗牙移植到自己的颌骨上——这些牙是从他的奴隶口中拔下来的。","正文"],["2011 英一 · 阅读 · Part B · 选项A","But the regular time it takes to get a doctoral degree in the humanities is nine years.","但取得人文学科博士学位通常需要九年。",""]],"nine.mp3",null],"nineteen":[["ˌnaɪnˈtiːn","ˌnɑɪnˈtin"],["中考","高中","CET4","考研"],[["复数","nineteens"],["adjective or noun","nineteenth",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["num.","十九",0]],[],"nineteen.mp3",{"r":[["词根","-teen = ten more than, 表示“十多（岁）”。"]],"d":[["nineteenth","第十九"]]}],"ninety":[["ˈnaɪn.ti","ˈnɑɪn·ti"],["中考","高中"],[["复数","nineties"],["adjective or noun","ninetieth",1]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["","九十",1],["","九十几；九十年代",0]],[["2009 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Besides the ninety or so learned ministers who came to Massachusetts churches in the decade after 1629, there were political leaders like John Winthrop, an educated gentleman, lawyer, and official of the Crown before he journeyed to Boston.","除1629年后十年间来到马萨诸塞各教会的大约九十位学识渊博的牧师外，还有约翰·温思罗普这样的政治领袖；他前往波士顿之前，曾是一位受过教育的绅士、律师和王室官员。","正文"]],"ninety.mp3",{"r":[["后缀","-ty = ten, 表示“十”，基数词后缀。"]],"d":[["ninetieth","第九十"]]}],"no":[["nəʊ","noʊ"],["中考","高中"],[["复数","noes"],["复数","nos"]],[202,5.0,44,148,19],[["exclam.","（用于否定的回答或陈述）不；没有；不是",3],["exclam.","（对某人所说的话感到惊讶）不，不要",0],["det.","没有；无",143],["det.","不准；禁止",4],["det.","（表示情况的反面）不是，并不",7],["det.","没有可能（做某事）",0],["adv.","（与 not 同义，用于形容词和副词前）不",44],["n.","否定的回答；作否定回答的人",0],["n.","（统称）投反对票者",0],["n.","不论…；无论…；不管…",1]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","There is no other institution, public or private, that can say the same.","没有其他任何公共或私人机构能作出同样的承诺。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","There’s no business like show business — but in Los Angeles, it feels like there’s no business at all.","没有哪个行业能比得上演艺业；可在洛杉矶，人们却感觉这个行业根本没有业务可做。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","There’s no need to back away from progress, as long as we’re equipped with the knowledge and tools to make sure AI remains a friend.","只要我们掌握足够的知识和工具，确保人工智能始终是我们的朋友，就没有必要拒绝进步。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","The animals could benefit from more research: Currently, there are no published genomes from donkeys located south of the Equator in Africa.","这些动物值得更多研究：目前，还没有发表过生活在非洲赤道以南的驴的基因组数据。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","“But if you ask a farmer in Brazil if he or she is concerned about climate change, they would say, ‘No, I am concerned about water,’ ” he says.","他说：“但如果你问一位巴西农民是否担心气候变化，他或她会说：‘不，我担心的是水。’”","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","“We have a mixed system, there is no spare capacity and as soon as there’s a hiccup on the line, the situation becomes highly complex,” he said.","他说：“我们的铁路是混合运行系统，没有富余运力；线路上稍有故障，情况就会变得非常复杂。”","正文"]],"no.mp3",null],"noise":[["nɔɪz","nɔɪz"],["中考","高中","IELTS"],[["复数","noises"],["原形","noise"],["第三人称单数","noises"],["现在分词","noising"],["过去式","noised"],["过去分词","noised"],["形容词","noiseless",1],["副词","noiselessly",1],["形容词","noiseful",1],["副词","noisefully",1]],[5,2.0,4,4,1],[["n.","声音；响声；噪音；吵闹声",4],["n.","噪声；干扰；电子干扰信号",1],["n.","干扰信息；垃圾信息",0]],[["2006 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","It’s all deliciously ironic when you consider that Shakespeare, who earns their living, was himself an actor (with a beard) and did his share of noise-making.","想想就觉得妙不可言的讽刺：养活他们的莎士比亚自己也是个演员（还留着胡子），也没少制造喧闹。","正文"],["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","A century ago, Freud formulated his revolutionary theory that dreams were the disguised shadows of our unconscious desires and fears; by the late 1970s, neurologists had switched to thinking of them as just “mental noise” — the random byproducts of the neural-repair work that goes on during sleep.","一个世纪前，弗洛伊德提出了革命性理论，认为梦是我们无意识欲望与恐惧的伪装投影；到了20世纪70年代末，神经学家转而认为梦不过是“精神噪声”，即睡眠期间神经修复活动产生的随机副产物。","正文"],["2000 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","This, in brief, is what the Futurist says: for a century, past conditions of life have been conditionally speeding up, till now we live in a world of noise and violence and speed.","简而言之，未来主义者的看法是：一个世纪以来，以往的生活状态一直在不断加速变化，以至于如今我们生活在一个充满喧嚣、暴力和速度的世界里。","正文"],["2000 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","But it is a little upsetting to read in the explanatory notes that a certain line describes a fight between a Turkish and a Bulgarian officer on a bridge off which they both fall into the river — and then to find that the line consists of the noise of their falling and the weights of the officers: “Pluff! Pluff! A hundred and eighty-five kilograms.”","可是，读到注释说某一行描写一名土耳其军官与一名保加利亚军官在桥上打斗，两人都从桥上落入河中，而那一行诗却只有落水声和军官们的体重：“扑通！扑通！一百八十五公斤。”这多少令人不安。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3 · 第34题 · 选项A","The expression “talking on the brush handle” in Paragraphs 3 and 6 refers to the act of making a loud noise.","第三段和第六段中“倚着扫帚柄聊天”这一说法，指的是制造很大噪声的行为。","选项"]],"noise.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nav-,naus-,naut- = ship, 表示“船”，naut- 引申为“海员”。"]],"d":[["noisy","1. adj. 嘈杂的；喧闹的；聒噪的 2. n. 响声；嘈杂声"],["noises","1. n. 噪音，响声，噪音（noise的复数形式） 2. v. 谣传（noise的第三人称单数形式）"],["noiseful","adj. 喧闹的，吵闹的"],["noiseless","adj. 没有噪音的;寂静的;不出声的"],["noisemaker","n. 发出大声音的人,会高声喧闹的人"]]}],"nonetheless":[["ˌnʌn.ðəˈles","ˌnʌn·ðəˈles"],["CET6","考研","TOEFL"],[],[4,1.5,4,2,0],[["adv.","尽管如此",4]],[["2012 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","Nonetheless, unification of sorts remains a major goal.","尽管如此，某种程度上的统一仍然是一个主要目标。","正文"],["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","A unity of objectives that nonetheless respect the varied peculiarities of each country.","目标上的团结，同时尊重各国不同的独特之处。","正文"],["2022 英一 · 完形","Though plants lack brains, the firing of electrical signals in their stems and leaves nonetheless triggered responses that hinted at consciousness, researchers previously reported.","研究人员此前报告说，尽管植物没有大脑，但其茎叶中发出的电信号仍会引发某些反应，暗示植物可能具有意识。",""],["2020 英一 · 完形","Even if families don’t sit down to eat together as frequently as before, millions of Britons will nonetheless have got a share this weekend of one of the nation’s great traditions: the Sunday roast.","尽管如今家人坐在一起吃饭不像过去那么频繁，但这个周末仍有数百万英国人享用了英国的一项伟大传统：周日烤肉餐。",""]],"nonetheless.mp3",{"r":[["前缀","non- 表示“不，非”。"],["后缀","-less 表形容词，“无…的，不…的”，和单词loss同源。"]],"d":[]}],"noodle":[["ˈnuː.dᵊl","ˈnu·dᵊl"],["中考","高中","考研"],[["复数","noodles"],["原形","noodle"],["第三人称单数","noodles"],["现在分词","noodling"],["过去式","noodled"],["过去分词","noodled"]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","面条",0]],[],"noodle.mp3",null],"noon":[["nuːn","nun"],["中考","高中"],[["复数","noons"]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","正午；中午",0]],[],"noon.mp3",null],"north":[["nɔːθ","nɔrθ"],["中考","高中"],[["复数","norths"],["名词","northness",1]],[14,3.0,13,11,0],[["n.","北；北方",1],["n.","北部；北部地区",1],["n.","（美国南北战争时与南方作战的）北部各州，北方",0],["n.","北方发达国家（尤指欧洲和北美各国）",0],["adj.","北方的；向北的；北部的",12],["adj.","北风的；北方吹来的",0],["adv.","向北；朝北",0],["adv.","某物以北",0],["adv.","超过",0]],[["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Their North American tree-ring fire-scar network (NAFSN) provided the basis for a study published last month.","他们建立的北美树木年轮火灾疤痕网络（NAFSN）成为上月发表的一项研究的基础。","正文"],["2025 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","ACE says it’s helped shrink the number of illegal streaming services in North America to 126, from more than 1,400 in 2018, aided in part by the MPA’s support for a 2020 federal law that made large-scale streaming of copyright material a serious crime.","ACE表示，它帮助北美的非法流媒体服务数量从2018年的1400多家降至126家；这部分得益于美国电影协会支持2020年出台的一项联邦法律，该法律将大规模通过流媒体非法播放受版权保护内容的行为定为严重犯罪。","正文"],["2021 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Equally, there is a sense that the travails of commuters in the South East, many of whom will face among the biggest rises, have received too much attention compared to those who must endure the relatively poor infrastructure of the Midlands and the North.","同样，也有人觉得，东南部通勤者（其中许多人将面临最大幅度的涨价）的困境，与那些不得不忍受英格兰中部和北部相对落后的基础设施的人相比，受到过多关注。","正文"],["2020 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","And if Sadiq Khan wins and extends it to the North and South Circular roads in 2021 as he intends, it is sure to spark intense opposition from the far larger number of motorists who will then be affected.","如果萨迪克·汗获胜，并按计划于2021年把超低排放区扩展到南北环路，那么受影响的司机将大幅增多，势必引发他们的强烈反对。","正文"],["2016 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","But the skills they learn — how to think logically through a problem and organize the results — apply to any coding language, said Deborah Seehorn, an education consultant for the state of North Carolina.","但北卡罗来纳州教育顾问德博拉·西霍恩说，他们学到的技能——如何有条理地分析问题并组织结果——适用于任何编程语言。","正文"],["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","These travelers to North America came in small, unmercifully overcrowded craft.","这些前往北美的旅行者乘坐的是狭小而拥挤不堪的船只。","正文"]],"north.mp3",null],"northeast":[["ˌnɔːθˈiːst","ˌnɔrθˈist"],["高中","CET4","CET6","考研"],[["复数","northeasts"]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","东北向，东北方",0],["adj. / adv.","在东北的;向东北的",0]],[],"northeast.mp3",{"r":[],"d":[["northeaster","东北风"],["northeastern","东北方"],["northeastward","东北"]]}],"northern":[["ˈnɔː.ðᵊn","ˈnɔrðərn"],["中考","高中","CET4","CET6","考研"],[["复数","northerns"]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["adj.","北方的；向北的；北部的",1]],[["2002 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Strengthening economic growth, at the same time as winter grips the northern hemisphere, could push the price higher still in the short term.","经济增长势头增强，而北半球同时进入寒冬，短期内可能进一步推高油价。","正文"]],"northern.mp3",{"r":[],"d":[["northerner","北方人"],["northernmost","北"]]}],"not":[["nɒt","nɑt"],["中考","高中"],[],[751,5.0,44,502,26],[["adv.","（构成动词 be、do 和 have 及情态动词 can 或 must 等的否定形式，常缩略为 n't）不，没有",501],["adv.","（否定后面的词或短语，或作否定的回答）不，没有",167],["adv.","（用于 hope、expect、believe 等动词后，作为否定的回答）不，没有",1],["adv.","（表示否定的可能性）否，或许不",7],["adv.","（拒绝或不允许）不",32],["adv.","不仅…而且…",43]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","The Silver Room Block Party, staged by Hyde Park community leader Eric Williams, announced it would not return in 2024.","由海德公园社区领袖埃里克·威廉姆斯举办的“银屋街区派对”宣布，2024 年不再举行。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","“We usually only get the human’s side of history through written accounts, but of course written history does not always record exactly how something happened.","“我们通常只能通过文字记载了解人类视角的历史；但文字记载当然并不总能准确记录事情的经过。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","We often hear people ask why we solicit donations at our entry points, especially when the city’s largest festivals like the Chicago Jazz Festival do not request donations.","人们常问，我们为什么在入口处募捐，尤其是像芝加哥爵士音乐节这样全市规模最大的节庆活动并不要求捐款。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","There will be no charge and you will never be asked to justify or explain yourself; you will simply be welcomed in, offered help if you need it, and left alone if you do not.","这里不收费，也绝不会要求你为到访说明理由；你只会受到欢迎，需要帮助时有人相助，不需要时也不会有人打扰。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Williams pointed to rising production costs and declining attendee donations as primary reasons the Silver Room Block Party could not continue, highlighting a reality that all street festival organizers face right now.","威廉姆斯指出，制作成本上升和参与者捐款减少，是银屋街区派对无法继续举办的主要原因；这也凸显了如今所有街头节庆组织者面临的现实。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","But, with this newfound connection, many of us share sensitive, sometimes highly confidential information, even though over a third of people don’t realise that AI platforms may not be very good at keeping our secrets...secret.","但有了这种新建立的联系，许多人会分享敏感、有时甚至高度机密的信息，尽管超过三分之一的人并不知道，人工智能平台可能并不擅长让我们的秘密……仍是秘密。","正文"]],"not.mp3",null],"notebook":[["ˈnəʊt.bʊk","ˈnoʊtˌbʊk"],["中考","高中","CET4","CET6","考研","IELTS"],[["复数","notebooks"]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["n.","笔记本",1],["n.","练习本",0],["n.","笔记本式计算机；笔记本电脑",0]],[["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","She draws on letters, diaries and fiction, and a 1939 field notebook of verbatim audience research by Winifred Gill.","她引用了书信、日记、小说，以及温妮弗雷德·吉尔1939年记录听众原话的实地调查笔记。","正文"]],"notebook.mp3",{"r":[["词根","not- = know, 表示“知道，注意”，和表示知道的词根 gn- 同源。"]],"d":[]}],"November":[["nəʊˈvem.bəʳ","noʊˈvem·bər"],["中考","高中","IELTS"],[["复数","Novembers"]],[3,1.5,3,3,0],[["n.","十一月",3]],[["2022 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","The performance was a creative call to action ahead of November’s United Nations Climate Change Conference in Glasgow, UK.","这场演出是在当年11月英国格拉斯哥举行的联合国气候变化大会之前，发出的一次富有创意的行动呼吁。","正文"],["2020 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Madrid was hailed as a public health guiding light last November when it rolled out ambitious restrictions on the most polluting cars.","去年11月，马德里出台雄心勃勃的措施限制污染最严重的汽车，因此被誉为公共卫生领域的引路人。","正文"],["2010 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Sales of contemporary art fell by two-thirds, and in the most overheated sector, they were down by nearly 90% in the year to November 2008.","当代艺术品销售额下降了三分之二；在最过热的领域，截至2008年11月的一年里，跌幅接近90%。","正文"]],"november.mp3",null],"now":[["naʊ","nɑʊ"],["中考","高中"],[["复数","nows"]],[169,5.0,43,145,2],[["adv.","现在；目前；此刻",160],["adv.","现在；从现在开始",4],["adv.","（表示厌烦）",0],["adv.","（改变话题或要对方做某事前，引起对方注意）喂，哎，嗨",2],["conj.","既然；由于",3]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Disruptions have become increasingly frequent with train delays now a fixture in Italian media coverage.","列车运行中断愈发频繁，晚点如今已成为意大利媒体报道中的常见话题。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","That’s why the California Film Commission and its Los Angeles counterpart, Film LA, now should act, before it’s too late.","正因如此，加利福尼亚电影委员会及其在洛杉矶的对应机构Film LA现在就该行动，以免为时已晚。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Now, researchers have used genomes of over 200 donkeys to trace their domestication back to a single event around 7,000 years ago in East Africa — about 3,000 years before humans tamed horses.","如今，研究人员利用200多头驴的基因组，将其驯化追溯到约7000年前东非发生的一次事件，比人类驯化马匹早了约3000年。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Ask people about public libraries and a certain image springs to mind: dusty, old-fashioned, the sort of place you enjoyed as a child but, rather like a British seaside town, would you go there now?","问起公共图书馆，人们脑海中往往浮现出某种印象：布满灰尘、老派过时，就像英国的海滨小镇一样，小时候去会很开心，可现在你还会去吗？","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Williams pointed to rising production costs and declining attendee donations as primary reasons the Silver Room Block Party could not continue, highlighting a reality that all street festival organizers face right now.","威廉姆斯指出，制作成本上升和参与者捐款减少，是银屋街区派对无法继续举办的主要原因；这也凸显了如今所有街头节庆组织者面临的现实。","正文"],["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Tip creep and tipflation are now further supplementing the income of many low-wage service workers.","如今，索取小费范围扩大和小费通胀又进一步补充了许多低薪服务业员工的收入。","正文"]],"now.mp3",null],"number":[["ˈnʌm.bəʳ","ˈnʌm·bər"],["中考","高中"],[["复数","numbers"],["原形","number"],["第三人称单数","numbers"],["现在分词","numbering"],["过去式","numbered"],["过去分词","numbered"],["形容词","numberable",1],["名词","numberer",1]],[185,5.0,44,94,7],[["n.","数字；数；数量",5],["n.","编号；序数",2],["n.","（电话等的）号码",4],["n.","数量；数额",89],["n.","一群人；许多人",1],["n.","期；号",0],["n.","一首歌，一段舞蹈（尤指演出的节目）",0],["n.","令人羡慕的东西",0],["n.","数（表示所叙述的人或事物是一个或多个）",0],["v.","标号；给…编号",80],["v.","总计；共计；数以…计",1],["v.","把…算作；（被）归入",0],["n.","几个，若干",1],["n.","数目；总数",2]],[["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","The number of libraries that have closed since 2010 is disputed.","自 2010 年以来关闭了多少家图书馆，至今仍有争议。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","The NAFSN sites experienced less than a quarter of the number of fires that would have been expected without fire suppression.","北美树木年轮火灾疤痕网络所研究地点的火灾次数，不到在没有人为扑火的情况下预期次数的四分之一。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","For questions 41-45, you are required to reorganize these paragraphs into a coherent text by choosing from the list A-H and filling them into the numbered boxes.","第41至45题要求你从A至H的列表中选择段落，填入编号方框，将它们重新排列成一篇连贯的文章。","正文"],["2026 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","As I visited libraries up and down the country, I was surprised to learn there are more than twice the number of libraries (2,892) as there are branches of McDonald’s.","走访全国各地的图书馆时，我惊讶地得知，图书馆共有 2,892 家，数量是麦当劳门店的两倍多。","正文"],["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","As the streamers’ emphasis changed from subscriber growth to profitability, prices for the services went up and the number of new shows went down to 481 released in 2023, with the number expected to dip into the 300s within a few years.","随着流媒体平台的重心从增加订户转向盈利，服务价格上涨，新推出的剧集则减少到2023年的481部；预计几年内还会降至300多部。","正文"],["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","And capacity in social care needs to be greater, to support the growing number of people living with long-term conditions.","社会照护的服务能力也需要提高，以支持越来越多患有长期疾病的人。","正文"]],"number.mp3",{"r":[["词根","numer- = number, 表示“数目”。"]],"d":[["outnumber","vt. 数量多于;比…多"],["numbered","adj. 有限的；计数的；时日无多的；编号的"],["renumber","vt. 重编号（等于renumerate）"],["numbering","编号"],["subnumber","子数"]]}],"narrowly":[["ˈnær.əʊ.li","ˈnær·ə·li"],[],[["复数","narrows"],["原形","narrow"],["第三人称单数","narrows"],["现在分词","narrowing"],["过去式","narrowed"],["过去分词","narrowed"],["比较级","narrower"],["最高级","narrowest"],["副词","narrowly",1],["名词","narrowness",1]],[2,1.0,2,1,1],[["adv.","勉强地；以毫厘之差",0],["adv.","狭隘地；严格地",2],["adv.","小心地；仔细地",0]],[["2001 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","If it did, it would open up its diversity program, now focused narrowly on race and gender, and look for reporters who differ broadly by outlook, values, education, and class.","如果它留意到了，就会拓宽目前仅聚焦种族和性别的多元化计划，寻找在观念、价值观、教育背景和阶层方面各不相同的记者。","正文"],["2022 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4 · 第36题 · 选项B","Scientists generally believe that the effects of ethics classes are narrowly interpreted.","科学家普遍认为，对伦理课效果的解读过于狭隘。","选项"]],"narrowly.mp3",{"r":[["后缀","-ly 表副词，通常缀于形容词后。"]],"d":[]}],"nasal":[["ˈneɪ.zᵊl","ˈneɪ·zəl"],["GRE"],[["复数","nasals"],["名词","nasality",1],["副词","nasally",1]],[1,0.5,1,0,0],[["adj.","鼻的；与鼻子相关的",1],["adj.","带鼻音的",0],["adj.","从鼻腔发出的；鼻音的",0]],[["2010 英二 · 完形","More than three million doses were to be made available in early October 2009, though most of those initial doses were of the FluMist nasal spray type, which is not recommended for pregnant women, people over 50 or those with breathing difficulties, heart disease or several other problems.","原定于2009年10月初供应300多万剂，不过最初这批疫苗大多是FluMist鼻喷剂型；这种剂型不推荐孕妇、50岁以上者，以及有呼吸困难、心脏病或其他几种疾病的人使用。",""]],"nasal.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nas-,naso- = nose, 表示“鼻”。 nas- 来自拉丁语，nos- 来自古英语，他们都源自原始印欧语 *nas-。"],["后缀","-al,-ial 表形容词，“…的”，一般缀于名词后。"]],"d":[["adnasal","adj. 近鼻的"],["nasalis","鼻肌"],["nasally","adv. 鼻声地；鼻地；护鼻地"],["nasality","n. 鼻音性；鼻声"],["nasalize","1. vi. 用鼻音发声 2. vt. 使鼻音化"]]}],"nationwide":[["ˌneɪ.ʃᵊnˈwaɪd","ˈneɪ·ʃənˈwɑɪd"],["高中","TOEFL"],[],[6,2.0,4,4,1],[["adjective, adverb","全国性的；遍及全国的；全国范围的",6]],[["2020 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","That is exactly what happened when Norway adopted a nationwide corporate gender quota.","挪威实行全国性的企业性别配额后，出现的正是这种情况。","正文"],["2019 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Sellers that use eBay and Etsy, which provide platforms for smaller sellers, also haven’t been collecting sales tax nationwide.","易贝和Etsy为小卖家提供交易平台；使用这些平台的卖家也一直没有在全国范围内征收销售税。","正文"],["2019 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Big chains have been collecting sales tax nationwide because they typically have physical stores in whatever state a purchase is being shipped to.","大型连锁企业一直在全国征收销售税，因为商品运往的州通常都有它们的实体店。","正文"],["2017 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Another nationwide concern is whether public funds from other agencies are going into construction in fire-prone districts.","另一个全国性的问题是，其他机构的公共资金是否正被用于在易发生火灾的地区修建建筑。","正文"],["2020 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3 · 第34题 · 选项C","Norway’s adoption of a nationwide corporate gender quota has led to the entry of unqualified candidates into the board.","挪威实施全国性的企业性别配额制度，导致不合格的候选人进入董事会。","题干"],["2003 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3 · 第33题 · 选项B","It can be inferred from paragraph 3 that there will soon be only one railroad company nationwide.","从第三段可以推断，全国很快将只剩一家铁路公司。","选项"]],"nationwide.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nat-,nai- = born, 表示“出生的”，来自古典拉丁语 gnasci，由词根 gen-（出生，产生）组成。"],["后缀","-ion,-ation,-ition 表名词，“行为、动作、状态、过程、结果；物品”等。"],["词根","vid-,vis- = separate, 表示“分开”。"]],"d":[]}],"native-born":[["ˌneɪtɪvˈbɔːn","ˌneɪtɪvˈbɔrn"],[],[],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["adj.","在本地出生的；因出生于某地而属于或与该地有关的",1]],[["2006 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","By 1996 foreign-born immigrants who had arrived before 1970 had a home ownership rate of 75.6 percent, higher than the 69.8 percent rate among native-born Americans.","截至1996年，1970年以前抵达美国的外国出生移民住房自有率为75.6%，高于美国本土出生者69.8%的住房自有率。","正文"]],"native-born.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nat-,nai- = born, 表示“出生的”，来自古典拉丁语 gnasci，由词根 gen-（出生，产生）组成。"],["后缀","-ive 表名词后缀，“人或物”。"]],"d":[]}],"naturalist":[["ˈnætʃ.ᵊr.ᵊl.ɪst","ˈnætʃ·ər·ə·lɪst"],["TOEFL"],[["复数","naturalists"]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["n.","博物学家",1]],[["2009 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","Coinciding with the groundbreaking theory of biological evolution proposed by British naturalist Charles Darwin in the 1860s, British social philosopher Herbert Spencer put forward his own theory of biological and cultural evolution.","19世纪60年代，英国博物学家查尔斯·达尔文提出开创性的生物进化论；与此同时，英国社会哲学家赫伯特·斯宾塞提出了自己的生物与文化进化理论。","正文"]],"naturalist.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nat-,nai- = born, 表示“出生的”，来自古典拉丁语 gnasci，由词根 gen-（出生，产生）组成。"],["后缀","-ture,-ature,-iture 表名词，通常在单词或词根以t结尾时使用，表示“一般状态，行为”。"],["后缀","-al,-ial 表形容词，“…的”，一般缀于名词后。"],["后缀","-ist 表名词，表示“信仰者，专家或从事某活动的人”。"]],"d":[]}],"nautical":[["ˈnɔː.tɪ.kᵊl","ˈnɔ·t̬ɪ·kəl"],["IELTS","GRE"],[["副词","nautically",1]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["adj.","航海的；海员的；船舶的",1]],[["2010 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","Dr. Kroo points out that the aircraft could be separated by several nautical miles, and would not be in the intimate groupings favoured by display teams like the Red Arrows.","克鲁博士指出，飞机之间可以相隔数海里，不会像“红箭”一类飞行表演队那样紧密编队。","正文"]],"nautical.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nav-,naus-,naut- = ship, 表示“船”，naut- 引申为“海员”。"],["后缀","-ical 表形容词，“…的”。"]],"d":[]}],"neatly":[["ˈniːt.li","ˈnit·li"],[],[["复数","neat"],["复数","neats"],["比较级","neater"],["最高级","neatest"],["副词","neatly",1],["名词","neatness",1],["形容词","unneat",1]],[36,4.0,23,0,0],[["adv.","简洁的；睿智的；灵巧的",0],["adv.","整洁地，整齐地",36]],[["2025 英一 · 写作 · Part B","You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET.","请在答题纸上工整书写。",""],["2019 英一 · 写作 · Part B · 第52题","Write your answer neatly on the ANSWER SHEET.","请在答题纸上工整地书写答案。",""],["2018 英一 · 写作 · Part A","You should write about 100 words neatly on the ANSEWER SHEET.","请在答题卡上工整地写约100词。",""],["2017 英一 · 阅读 · Part C","Your translation should be written neatly on the ANSWER SHEET.","请在答题卡上工整地写出译文。",""],["2013 英二 · 翻译","My mind seems to be able to cope and the information is stored away neatly.","我的大脑似乎应付得来，还能把信息整齐地储存起来。",""],["2012 英一 · 写作 · Part B","You should write neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2.","请在答题卡2上工整书写。",""]],"neatly.mp3",{"r":[["后缀","-ly 表副词，通常缀于形容词后。"]],"d":[]}],"necessarily":[["ˈnes.ə.ser.ɪl.i","ˌnes·əˈseər·ə·li"],["CET4","CET6"],[],[11,2.5,9,7,0],[["adv.","必然地；不可避免地",11]],[["2020 英二 · 阅读 · Part B","Jokes that work on one person won’t necessarily land with another.","对一个人奏效的玩笑，未必也能逗笑另一个人。","正文"],["2018 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Nothing is necessarily gained by forcing students to learn geometry at a graffitied desk stuck with generations of discarded chewing gum.","强迫学生坐在满是涂鸦、粘着几代人丢弃的口香糖的课桌前学几何，并不一定能让他们有所收获。","正文"],["2017 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","It’s not necessarily a bad thing, but depending on the school, it can be costly to make up credits after switching too late in the game.","转专业本身未必是坏事，但要看学校的规定；如果转得太晚，补修学分可能很费钱。","正文"],["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","It doesn’t then necessarily follow that one kind of reading is fuller, more advanced and more worthwhile than another.","因此，不能必然断定某一种阅读方式比另一种更完整、更高级、更有价值。","正文"],["2013 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","The problem is not necessarily the amount of available funding.","问题未必在于现有资金的多少。","正文"],["2008 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","“It’s not necessarily that women don’t cope as well.","“这未必是说女性应对压力的能力较差。","正文"]],"necessarily.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neg- = deny, 表示“否认”，原始印欧语形式为 *ne- (no, not)，和词根 un- 同源。"],["词根","ced-,ceed-,cess- = go away; withdraw, yield, 表示“走开，撤退，屈服”。来自拉丁语。"],["后缀","-ary 表形容词，“…的”。"],["后缀","-ly 表副词，通常缀于形容词后。"]],"d":[]}],"needlessly":[["ˈniːd.ləs.li","ˈniːd.ləs.li"],[],[["副词","needlessly",1],["名词","needlessness",1]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["adv.","不必要的；可以避免的",1]],[["2002 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","“Large numbers of physicians seem unconcerned with the pain their patients are needlessly and predictably suffering”, to the extent that it constitutes “systematic patient abuse”.","“许多医生似乎对患者正在遭受的、不必要且完全可以预见的痛苦漠不关心”，其严重程度已构成“系统性的患者虐待”。","正文"]],"needlessly.mp3",null],"needy":[["ˈniː.di","ˈnid·i"],["TOEFL","GRE"],[["比较级","needier"],["最高级","neediest"],["名词","neediness",1]],[1,0.5,1,0,0],[["adj.","缺乏生活必需品的；贫困的",1],["adj.","穷困的人",0],["adj.","缺乏自信的；需要精神支持的",0]],[["2019 英一 · 阅读 · Part B · 选项G","Now we can understand each other’s positions and recognize our shared values, since we both care about needy workers.","这时，我们就能理解彼此的立场，认识到我们拥有共同的价值观，因为双方都关心有需要的劳动者。",""]],"needy.mp3",{"r":[["后缀","-y 表形容词，加在名词后变成形容词。"]],"d":[["neediness","n. 穷困,贫穷"]]}],"negligence":[["ˈneɡ.lɪ.dʒᵊns","ˈnɛɡlədʒəns"],["TOEFL","IELTS","GRE"],[["复数","negligences"]],[1,0.5,1,0,1],[["n.","疏忽；失职；失误；过失",1]],[["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2 · 第30题 · 选项A","The author associates the issue of global warming with that of smoking because they both suffered from the government’s negligence.","作者将全球变暖问题与吸烟问题联系起来，是因为这两个问题都因政府的疏忽而受到不利影响。","选项"]],"negligence.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neg- = deny, 表示“否认”，原始印欧语形式为 *ne- (no, not)，和词根 un- 同源。"],["词根","lect-,lig-,leg- = choose, gather, 表示“选择，收集”，来自拉丁语。"],["后缀","-ence 表名词，“性质，状态”。"]],"d":[]}],"netball":[["ˈnet.bɔːl","ˈnet.bɑːl"],[],[],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["n.","（女子）无挡板篮球",1]],[["2017 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","If there is a role for government, it should really be getting involved in providing common goods — making sure there is space for playing fields and the money to pave tennis and netball courts, and encouraging the provision of all these activities in schools.","如果政府要发挥作用，就应该真正参与提供公共资源：确保有运动场地，拨款铺设网球场和无挡板篮球场，并鼓励学校开展所有这些活动。","正文"]],"netball.mp3",{"r":[["词根","ball-,bol- = ball 球，球形"]],"d":[]}],"neural":[["ˈnjʊə.rəl","ˈnʊrəl"],[],[["副词","neurally",1]],[2,1.0,1,1,1],[["adj.","神经的；神经系统的",2]],[["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","A century ago, Freud formulated his revolutionary theory that dreams were the disguised shadows of our unconscious desires and fears; by the late 1970s, neurologists had switched to thinking of them as just “mental noise” — the random byproducts of the neural-repair work that goes on during sleep.","一个世纪前，弗洛伊德提出了革命性理论，认为梦是我们无意识欲望与恐惧的伪装投影；到了20世纪70年代末，神经学家转而认为梦不过是“精神噪声”，即睡眠期间神经修复活动产生的随机副产物。","正文"],["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3 · 第31题 · 选项D","Researchers have come to believe that dreams are a random outcome of neural repairs.","研究人员如今认为，梦是神经修复过程中随机产生的结果。","选项"]],"neural.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neur-,nerv- = nerve 神经，勇气"],["后缀","-al,-ial 表形容词，“…的”，一般缀于名词后。"]],"d":[["neuralward","向神经"],["neuralization","神经化"]]}],"neurology":[["njʊəˈrɒl.ə.dʒi","nʊˈrɑl·ə·dʒi"],["考研","GRE"],[["复数","neurologies"],["形容词","neurological",1],["副词","neurologically",1]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["n.","神经病学；神经学",1]],[["2007 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","How much of intelligence can be specified, and how much can we learn about it from neurology, genetics, computer science and other fields?","智力有多少可以被明确界定？神经学、遗传学、计算机科学及其他领域又能让我们对智力了解多少？","正文"]],"neurology.mp3",{"r":[["词根","neur-,nerv- = nerve 神经，勇气"],["后缀","-logy,-logist,-logical = science, 表示“科学，学科”，由词根 log-, 说，引申而来；-logy 作为词缀表示...学，-logist 作为词缀表示...学家, -logical 作为词缀表示...学的。"]],"d":[]}],"neuroscientist":[["ˌnjʊə.rəʊˈsaɪ.ən.tɪst","ˌnʊr.oʊˈsaɪ.ən.tɪst"],[],[["复数","neuroscientists"],["形容词","neuroscientific",1]],[5,2.0,5,3,0],[["n.","神经科学家（研究大脑和神经系统结构与功能的科学家）",5]],[["2020 英一 · 阅读 · Part B","Neuroscientist Bonnie Auyeung found that the hormone oxytocin increased the amount of eye contact from men toward the interviewer during a brief interview when the direction of their gaze was recorded.","神经科学家邦妮·奥耶恩发现，在一次简短访谈中记录受访男性的目光方向时，催产素会增加他们看向采访者的目光接触次数。","正文"],["2019 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Just how people think is still far too complex to be understood, let alone reproduced, says David Eagleman, a Stanford University neuroscientist.","斯坦福大学神经科学家戴维·伊格尔曼说，人类究竟如何思考，仍复杂得远非我们所能理解，更不用说复制了。","正文"]],"neuroscientist.mp3",null],"newsprint":[["ˈnjuːz.prɪnt","ˈnuzprɪnt"],[],[["复数","newsprints"]],[2,1.0,2,2,0],[["n.","新闻纸；白报纸",2]],[["2016 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","There will eventually come a day when The New York Times ceases to publish stories on newsprint.","终有一天，《纽约时报》将不再发行纸质报纸。","正文"],["2010 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","We are even farther removed from the unfocused newspaper reviews published in England between the turn of the 20th century and the eve of World War Ⅱ, at a time when newsprint was dirt-cheap and stylish arts criticism was considered an ornament to the publications in which it appeared.","至于二十世纪初至第二次世界大战前夕英国报纸上那些主题散漫的评论，我们就更觉得遥远了：那时新闻纸便宜得惊人，而文笔优雅的艺术评论被视为所载报刊的点缀。","正文"]],"newsprint.mp3",{"r":[["词根","press-,prin-,prim- = press, 表示“挤压”。"]],"d":[]}],"newsroom":[["ˈnjuːz.ruːm","ˈnuz·rum"],[],[["复数","newsrooms"]],[6,2.0,3,5,1],[["n.","（报社、电台或电视台的）新闻编辑室",6]],[["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","One of the astonishing revelations was how little Rebekah Brooks knew of what went on in her newsroom, how little she thought to ask and the fact that she never inquired how the stories arrived.","一个令人震惊的发现是，丽贝卡·布鲁克斯对自己编辑部发生的事所知甚少，她很少想到要追问，而且从未询问报道是如何得来的。","正文"],["2011 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","The American Society of News Editors reckons that 13,500 newsroom jobs have gone since 2007.","美国新闻编辑协会估计，自2007年以来，新闻编辑部已经失去13500个岗位。","正文"],["2011 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","The whirlwind that swept through newsrooms harmed everybody, but much of the damage has been concentrated in areas where newspapers are least distinctive.","席卷新闻编辑部的风暴伤及所有人，但损失主要集中在报纸最缺乏独特性的领域。","正文"],["2001 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","In other words, there is a conventional story line in the newsroom culture that provides a backbone and a ready-made narrative structure for otherwise confusing news.","换言之，新闻编辑室文化中存在一套惯用的叙事模式，为原本纷繁难解的新闻提供主线和现成的叙事结构。","正文"],["2001 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","There exists a social and cultural disconnect between journalists and their readers, which helps explain why the “standard templates” of the newsroom seem alien to many readers.","记者与读者之间存在社会和文化上的隔阂，这有助于解释为什么新闻编辑室的“标准模板”让许多读者觉得陌生。","正文"],["2011 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2 · 第28题 · 选项B","Compared with their American counterparts, Japanese newspapers are much more stable because they have more balanced newsrooms.","与美国报纸相比，日本报纸稳定得多，因为它们拥有更加均衡的新闻编辑部。","选项"]],"newsroom.mp3",{"r":[["词根","room,rum- 表示“空间”。"]],"d":[]}],"newsstand":[["ˈnjuːz.stænd","ˈnuzˌstænd"],["TOEFL"],[["复数","newsstands"]],[2,1.0,1,2,0],[["n.","书亭；书摊",0],["n.","报摊；书报亭",0],["n.","报摊，报亭，报刊出售处",2]],[["2011 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Practically every week features at least one celebrity mom, or mom-to-be, smiling on the newsstands.","几乎每周，报刊亭的刊物上都会出现至少一位面带微笑的明星母亲或准母亲。","正文"],["2011 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","The magazine cover showing an attractive mother holding a cute baby is hardly the only Madonna-and-child image on newsstands this week.","本周报刊亭里，封面上那位抱着可爱婴儿的迷人母亲，绝非唯一一幅“圣母与圣子”式的画面。","正文"]],"newsstand.mp3",{"r":[["词根","st-,sta-,stat-,stan-,stant-,stin- = stand, 表示“站、立”。"]],"d":[]}],"niche":[["niːʃ","nɪtʃ"],["TOEFL","GRE"],[["复数","niches"],["原形","niche"],["第三人称单数","niches"],["现在分词","niching"],["过去式","niched"],["过去分词","niched"]],[3,1.5,3,3,0],[["n.","舒适或称心的工作（或生活等）",0],["n.","“利基”，商机，市场补缺（针对特定消费者群体的市场需求）",1],["n.","壁龛；（山体）凹进的地方",0],["n.","生态位（一种生物在群落中的地位或作用）",0],["adj.","只令少数人感兴趣、只面向少数人或只影响少数人的；小众的",2]],[["2026 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","And while it is wonderful to take a walk with anything in your headphones, infinite choice encourages us to shrink into niche interests and sympathetic beliefs.","而且，虽然散步时耳机里想听什么就听什么很美妙，无限的选择却会促使我们缩进兴趣和观点相近的小圈子。","正文"],["2024 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Solar panels had few niche uses until they became cheap; now they are transforming the global energy system.","太阳能电池板在变得便宜之前只有少数专门用途；如今，它们正改变全球能源体系。","正文"],["2022 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","In barely more than a decade, organic eggs went from being dismissed as a niche product in natural foods stores to being sold at Walmart.","短短十余年，有机鸡蛋从天然食品店里被人看轻的小众商品，变成了沃尔玛货架上的商品。","正文"]],"niche.mp3",null],"nobility":[["nəʊˈbɪl.ə.ti","noʊˈbɪl·ɪ·t̬i"],["IELTS"],[["复数","nobilities"]],[2,1.0,1,0,1],[["n.","贵族",2],["n.","高贵的品质",0]],[["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1 · 第23题 · 选项D","Which of the following is shown to be odd, according to Paragraph 4? The nobility’s adherence to their privileges.","根据第四段，下列哪一点显得奇怪？贵族坚持保有自己的特权。","选项"],["2015 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1 · 第23题 · 选项B","Which of the following is shown to be odd, according to Paragraph 4? The role of the nobility in modern democracies.","根据第四段，下列哪一点显得奇怪？贵族在现代民主制度中的作用。","选项"]],"nobility.mp3",{"r":[["后缀","-ity 表名词，指具备某种性质。"],["词根","gn-,gnos-,gnor- = know, 表示“知道”，来自拉丁语。"]],"d":[]}],"noisily":[["ˈnɔɪ.zᵊl.i","ˈnɔɪ.zᵊl.i"],["高中"],[["比较级","noisier"],["最高级","noisiest"],["副词","noisily",1],["名词","noisiness",1]],[1,0.5,1,0,0],[["adv.","吵闹地，喧哗地，嘈杂地",1]],[["2004 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2 · 第29题 · 选项B","What does the author mean by “most people are literally having a ZZZ” (Paragraph 5)? They are noisily dozing off.","作者说“大多数人确实已经呼呼大睡了”（第五段）是什么意思？他们正在打瞌睡，发出鼾声。","选项"]],"noisily.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nav-,naus-,naut- = ship, 表示“船”，naut- 引申为“海员”。"],["后缀","-y 表形容词，加在名词后变成形容词。"],["后缀","-ly 表副词，通常缀于形容词后。"]],"d":[]}],"nonconformist":[["ˌnɒn.kənˈfɔː.mɪst","ˌnɑn·kəmˈfɔr·mɪst"],["TOEFL","GRE"],[["复数","nonconformists"]],[1,0.5,1,0,0],[["n.","（英格兰和威尔士）不从国教者，不遵奉圣公会的新教教徒",0],["n.","不遵循传统规范的人；不认同主流思想的人",0],["adj.","（英格兰和威尔士）不从国教者，不遵奉圣公会的新教教徒",0],["adj.","不遵循传统规范的人；不认同主流思想的人",1]],[["2003 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1 · 第25题 · 选项B","Straitford is most proud of its nonconformist image.","Straitford最引以为傲的是它不墨守成规的形象。","选项"]],"nonconformist.mp3",{"r":[["前缀","non- 表示“不，非”。"],["前缀","co-,com-,con-,col-,cor- 来自拉丁语介词com，表示“与...一起，一起（with, together）”，或仅做强调。"],["词根","form- = shape, 表示“形状”，来自拉丁语 formare \"to shape, give form to\" 及 forma \"form\"。"],["后缀","-ist 表名词，表示“信仰者，专家或从事某活动的人”。"]],"d":[]}],"non-standard":[["ˌnɒnˈstæn.dəd","ˌnɑːnˈstæn.dɚd"],[],[],[2,1.0,1,1,1],[["adj.","非标准的；不规范的",2],["adj.","（尺寸、型号等）不标准的，非常用的",0]],[["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","As a linguist, he acknowledges that all varieties of human language, including non-standard ones like Black English, can be powerfully expressive — there exists no language or dialect in the world that cannot convey complex ideas.","作为语言学家，他承认，人类语言的所有变体，包括黑人英语这样的非标准变体，都能有力地表达思想：世上没有任何一种语言或方言不能传达复杂观念。","正文"],["2005 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4 · 第38题 · 选项C","To which of the following statements would McWhorter most likely agree? Non-standard varieties of human language are just as entertaining.","麦克沃特最可能赞同以下哪种说法？人类语言的非标准变体同样有趣。","选项"]],"non-standard.mp3",null],"nonverbal":[["ˌnɒnˈvɜː.bᵊl","ˌnɑnˈvərbl"],["TOEFL"],[["副词","nonverbally",1]],[2,1.0,1,2,0],[["adj.","不用词语或语言的；非言语的",2],["adj.","不能或似乎不能使用口语交流的",0]],[["2017 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","She found that mothers who used devices during the exercise started 20 percent fewer verbal and 39 percent fewer nonverbal interactions with their children.","她发现，在任务中使用设备的母亲，与孩子进行的语言互动少了 20%，非语言互动少了 39%。","正文"],["2017 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","“Parents don’t have to be exquisitely present at all times, but there needs to be a balance and parents need to be responsive and sensitive to a child’s verbal or nonverbal expressions of an emotional need,” says Radesky.","拉德斯基说：“父母不必时时刻刻都全神贯注地陪伴孩子，但必须把握平衡，并对孩子用语言或非语言方式表达的情感需求作出及时而敏锐的回应。”","正文"]],"nonverbal.mp3",{"r":[["前缀","non- 表示“不，非”。"],["词根","verb- = word, 表示“词语”。"],["后缀","-al,-ial 表形容词，“…的”，一般缀于名词后。"]],"d":[]}],"notably":[["ˈnəʊ.tə.bli","ˈnoʊt̮əbli"],["TOEFL"],[],[5,2.0,3,4,0],[["adv.","尤其；特别",2],["adv.","极大程度上；非常",1],["adv.","明显地；显然；值得注意地",2]],[["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Notably, tipping primarily benefits some of these workers, such as waiters, but not others, such as cooks and dishwashers.","值得注意的是，小费主要让其中一些员工受益，比如服务员，却不能惠及厨师和洗碗工等其他员工。","正文"],["2025 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","Notably, Broadway stands out as one of the few areas in NYC that defies the grid-based system applied to the rest of the city, cutting a diagonal across parts of the city.","值得注意的是，百老汇是纽约市少数不遵循城市其他区域所采用的网格状布局的道路之一，它斜穿城市的部分地区。","正文"],["2018 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2","While the rest of the world takes the lead, notably China and Europe, the United States is also seeing a remarkable shift.","世界其他地区，尤其是中国和欧洲，走在前面，而美国也正在经历显著的转变。","正文"],["2008 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 3","Growth, which rarely continues beyond the age of 20, demands calories and nutrients — notably, protein — to feed expanding tissues.","身体生长很少持续到20岁以后；它需要热量和营养物质，尤其是蛋白质，来供给不断扩张的组织。","正文"],["2018 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 2 · 第27题 · 选项A","According to Paragraph 3, the use of renewable energy in America is progressing notably.","根据第三段，美国在使用可再生能源方面取得了显著进展。","选项"]],"notably.mp3",{"r":[["词根","not- = know, 表示“知道，注意”，和表示知道的词根 gn- 同源。"],["后缀","-able 一般缀于动词后，构成形容词，表示“可…的，能…”。"],["后缀","-ably,-ibly 表副词，“能…地”。"]],"d":[]}],"noteworthy":[["ˈnəʊtˌwɜː.ði","ˈnoʊtˌwɜr·ði"],["考研"],[["副词","noteworthily",1],["名词","noteworthiness",1],["形容词","unnoteworthy",1]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["adj.","值得注意的；显著的；重要的",1]],[["2007 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","If you were to examine the birth certificates of every soccer player in 2006’s World Cup tournament, you would most likely find a noteworthy quirk: elite soccer players are more likely to have been born in the earlier months of the year than in the later months.","如果查看2006年世界杯每位足球运动员的出生证明，你很可能会发现一个值得注意的现象：优秀足球运动员出生于年初几个月的概率高于年末几个月。","正文"]],"noteworthy.mp3",{"r":[["词根","not- = know, 表示“知道，注意”，和表示知道的词根 gn- 同源。"],["词根","worth- = value, 表示“价值”，和表示“转”的词根 ver- 同源"],["后缀","-y 表形容词，加在名词后变成形容词。"]],"d":[["noteworthily","adv. 显著的"]]}],"notification":[["ˌnəʊ.tɪ.fɪˈkeɪ.ʃᵊn","ˌnoʊt̮əfəˈkeɪʃn"],["CET6"],[["复数","notifications"]],[1,0.5,1,1,0],[["n.","通知；通告；告示",1]],[["2004 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","Redmon chose the keywords legal, intellectual property and Washington, D. C. Three weeks later, he got his first notification of an opening.","雷德蒙选用了“法律”“知识产权”和“华盛顿特区”作为关键词。三周后，他收到了第一条职位空缺通知。","正文"]],"notification.mp3",{"r":[["后缀","-ion,-ation,-ition 表名词，“行为、动作、状态、过程、结果；物品”等。"],["词根","not- = know, 表示“知道，注意”，和表示知道的词根 gn- 同源。"],["后缀","-fy,-ify 缀于名词或形容词后，构成表示“使成…”“…化”“作成…”等意思的动词"]],"d":[]}],"nova":[["ˈnəʊ.və","ˈnoʊvə；ˈnoʊvi"],["GRE"],[["复数","novas"],["复数","novae"],["形容词","novalike",1]],[0,0.0,0,0,0],[["n.","新星（短期内突然变得很亮）",0]],[],"nova.mp3",{"r":[["词根","nov- = new, 表示“新的”。"]],"d":[["supernova","天］超新星"]]}],"nudge":[["nʌdʒ","nʌdʒ"],["GRE"],[["复数","nudges"],["原形","nudge"],["第三人称单数","nudges"],["现在分词","nudging"],["过去式","nudged"],["过去分词","nudged"],["名词","nudger",1]],[2,1.0,2,2,0],[["v.","（用肘）轻推，轻触",0],["v.","（朝某方向）轻推，渐渐推动",1],["v.","用胳膊肘挤开往前走",0],["v.","（使）达到，接近",0],["n.","（肘部的）轻推，碰",0],["n.","温和的劝导或促动；这种引导行为",1]],[["2022 英二 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 4","And if real, she notes, it might be reversible by another nudge: “Easy come, easy go.”","她指出，如果效果真实存在，也可能被另一次轻微干预逆转：“来得容易，去得也快。”","正文"],["2020 英一 · 阅读 · Part A · Text 1","They transform the aspirations of the people who live there; they nudge the self-image of the city into a bolder and more optimistic light.","他们改变当地居民的抱负，也推动这座城市以更大胆、更乐观的眼光看待自己。","正文"]],"nudge.mp3",null]};